PVD("japan_ndp_2024-2024",{"docs":["","JPN Honebuto 2024 English"],"s":{"1":[[1,"3","7","Wage Increase Promotion Measures","Encouraging wage increases",""],[1,"3","7","Price Pass-Through Measures","Price-pass-through measures",""],[1,"6","4","Wage Growth Extension to SMEs and Regional Economies","extend the momentum of robust wage increases achieved in this year's spring labor-management negotiations to sectors beyond those covered by the negotiations, such as small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and regional economies",""],[1,"7","2","Labor Cost Pass-Through Guidelines Dissemination","activities to disseminate guidelines for passing labor costs onto product prices",""],[1,"7","2","Cross-Sectoral Price Pass-Through and Business Earning Support","To ensure appropriate price pass-through across the entire supply chain, including industries with multi-layered transactional structures, both the public and private sectors will further strengthen their efforts.",""],[1,"7","3","Industry-Specific Wage Price Pass-Through Measures","the government will work on price pass-through measures tailored to the realities of different industries and sectors, including smoothing the transfer of labor costs onto product prices",""],[1,"7","3","Business Practices Reform for Wage Growth","implementing bold reforms of business practices",""],[1,"7","3","Sectoral Wage Increase Support","we will provide detailed support for wage increases in sectors such as healthcare and welfare",""],[1,"7","3","Minimum Wage Increase","raise the minimum wage",""],[1,"10","2","Structural Wage Increase Policy","we will establish structural wage increases across society",""],[1,"13","1","Structural Wage Increase Policy","we will cement structural wage increases",""],[1,"15","3","Wage Increase Support Measures","we will vigorously implement support measures for wage increases",""],[1,"15","3","Healthcare and Welfare Wage Increase Measures","take steps to steadily raise wages in fields such as healthcare and welfare",""],[1,"15","4","National Minimum Wage Increase Policy","the government aims to raise the national weighted average minimum wage to 1,500 yen per hour by the mid-2030s",""],[1,"15","4","Regional Minimum Wage Disparity Reduction","Efforts will continue to be made to redress regional disparities, through increasing the ratio of the lowest minimum wage to the highest",""],[1,"16","2","Healthcare Worker Wage Increase Financing Mechanism","the government will utilize mechanisms such as the base-up evaluation fees, introduced as a part of FY2024 revision of medical service fees, to achieve wage increases for workers.",""],[1,"16","2","Healthcare Wage Increase Monitoring Mechanism","we will continue efforts towards sustainable wage increases by monitoring the status of wage hikes5",""],[1,"16","2","Employer Wage Increase Engagement","persistently urging employers to raise wages.",""],[1,"16","3","Construction and Logistics Wage Guidelines","the government will quickly prepare guidelines based on the revised Construction Business Act6 and the revised Logistics Act7",""],[1,"16","3","Private-Sector Labor Cost and Freight Standards","ensure that labor cost standards and standard freight charges are applied not only to transactions with the national and local governments but also to those between private companies",""],[1,"16","3","Public Construction Labor Unit Price Reform","appropriately set labor unit prices in public construction design",""],[1,"16","3","Truck Worker Conditions and Fair Transactions Initiative","the government will promote necessary initiatives to improve workers' conditions and ensure fair transactions by strengthening the functions of the Truck G-Men, etc.",""],[1,"16","3","Passenger Motor Carrier Fare System Awareness","the government will raise awareness of the revised fare system8",""],[1,"16","4","Security Industry Wage Increase Promotion Measure","To promote wage increases in the security industry, the government will encourage the price-pass-through of labor costs through measures such as requesting the sector to revise its voluntary action plans.",""],[1,"17","1","Sectoral Cost Index Establishment Mechanism","the government will promptly establish cost indices based on a forum for public-private discussions to ensure rational price formation that considers factors such as raw material costs and labor expenses.",""],[1,"17","1","New Price Formation Systems Legislation","we aim to submit legislation for new systems to the regular session of the National Diet in 2025.",""],[1,"18","7","Structured Price-Pass-Through Enforcement Initiative","The government will realize “structured price-pass-through” to establish appropriate price-pass-through across the supply chain as a new commercial practice.",""],[1,"19","1","Subcontract G-Men Enforcement Measures","through measures such as the Subcontract G-Men",""],[1,"19","1","Subcontract Act Amendment Consideration","consider amendments to the Subcontract Act",""],[1,"19","1","Price Negotiation Guidelines Compliance Initiative","We will ensure that the Guidelines on Price Negotiation for Appropriate Pass-through of Labor Costs 12 are fully recognized and adhered to by stakeholders.",""],[1,"19","1","Price Pass-Through Effectiveness Monitoring","The government will investigate whether initiatives to facilitate price pass-through are being effectively carried out",""],[1,"19","1","Industry Self-Regulation Improvement Plans","will request these industries to formulate or revise self-regulation plans and/or consider improvement measures",""],[1,"19","1","Industry-Tailored Price Negotiation Format","the government will encourage stakeholders to modify and utilize this format tailored to the characteristics of their respective industries.",""],[1,"19","1","Partnership Building Declaration Implementation","The government will encourage more companies to issue a Partnership Building Declaration and will take measures to ensure that these declarations are effectively implemented.",""],[1,"19","1","Supply Chain Payment Period Reduction Roadmap","The government will prepare a roadmap for initiatives aimed at shortening payment periods for bills, such as promissory notes, transitioning to cash payments, and phasing out the use of promissory notes across the entire supply chain.",""],[1,"19","3","Public Contract Modification Budget Provision","When placing orders14, government agencies will secure the necessary budget to accept contract modifications within the fiscal year to ensure that contractors can pass on increases in labor costs and other expenses to the ordering parties if such cost increases occur.",""],[1,"19","3","Minimum Price Limit Regulation Promotion","The government will promote the appropriate use of the minimum price limit regulations and other measures.",""],[1,"91","3","SME and Local Entity Wage Increase Initiative","realize the trend of wage increases in the spring labor-management negotiations even at SMEs, small businesses, and local entities, etc.",""],[1,"91","3","Medical and Long-Term Care Wage Increases","raising wages in the field of medical and long-term care based on public prices",""],[1,"91","3","Minimum Wage Increase Policy","raising minimum wages",""],[1,"91","3","Personal and Resident Income Tax Reduction","introducing flat-amount cut of personal income tax and individual resident tax",""],[1,"15","2","Wage Increase Promotion Policy","Encouraging wage increases",""]],"2":[[1,"3","7","Trinity Labor Market Reform","Trinity labor market reforms",""],[1,"7","3","Trinity Labor Market Reform","the government will pursue trinity labor market reforms, focusing on strengthening reskilling and upskilling efforts targeting all generations",""],[1,"7","3","Job-Based Personnel Management Introduction","the government will promote the introduction of job-based personnel management (job-based pay) tailored to the circumstances of individual companies",""],[1,"7","3","Employment Policy Shift toward Labor Mobility","shift the direction of employment policies from job retention towards facilitating labor mobility into growth sectors",""],[1,"12","4","Human Capital Investment","investing in human capital",""],[1,"12","4","Lifelong Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","advance lifelong reskilling and upskilling for all generations",""],[1,"17","4","Workforce Reskilling and Upskilling Initiatives","The government promotes reskilling and upskilling initiatives targeting all generations, thereby supporting the enhancement of skills among the workforce.",""],[1,"17","5","Educational Training Benefits System Enhancement","The government will enhance the educational training benefits system, including raising the benefit rate, and expand the qualifications and courses eligible for benefits.",""],[1,"17","5","Educational Training Leave Livelihood Benefit Scheme","A new benefit scheme will be established to support the livelihood of trainees during educational training leave.",""],[1,"17","5","Group Certification Course Eligibility Expansion","The government will consider adding certain skill acquisition courses for this certification to those eligible for benefits within 2024.",""],[1,"17","5","Cross-Industry Group Certification Promotion","We will promote the utilization of the Group Certification system across various industries (such as construction, logistics, and tourism) through cooperation with relevant ministries and industry associations.",""],[1,"17","6","Regional Executive Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","The government will expand the reskilling and upskilling program using regional platforms for industry-academia-government collaboration to include business owners and executives, aiming to support the capacity building of around 5,000 individuals in this category by 2029.",""],[1,"17","6","University-Industry Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","The government will establish a reskilling and upskilling program in collaboration with universities and industries to equip participants with cutting-edge knowledge and strategic thinking.",""],[1,"17","7","Job-Based Personnel Management Guidelines","The government will publish the Job-Based Personnel Management Guidelines this summer, featuring case studies of various companies that have already adopted this management, to support companies in considering the introduction of this system in accordance with their respective circumstances.",""],[1,"17","8","Public and Private Job Information Integration","the government will advance the organization and integration of public and private information on job openings, job seekers, and career advancement",""],[1,"17","8","Reskilling and Upskilling Information Platform","in FY 2025, we will initiate the development of a platform to visualize various information, including reskilling and upskilling programs and policy details",""],[1,"18","1","National Labor Market Reform Movement","The government will launch a national movement to advance labor market reform.",""],[1,"18","1","National Labor Market Reform Conference","we will consider convening a national conference.",""],[1,"20","5","Automation Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","The government will promote initiatives for reskilling and upskilling aimed at developing frontline workers with capabilities in using automation technologies.",""],[1,"20","6","Flexible Temporary Staffing Using Multiple Jobs","temporary staffing that capitalizes on side jobs and multiple jobs, etc.",""],[1,"20","6","Regional DX Talent Matching Support","We will also provide support to facilitate matching between DX talent, etc. of large enterprises in various regions and LMEs and SMEs or local governments.",""],[1,"20","6","Regional Talent Development and Retention Collaboration","The government will support local governments and regional business support organizations in collaborating to secure, nurture, and retain talent.",""]],"3":[[1,"18","6","Government Digital Work Environment Improvement","digital environment improvements",""],[1,"18","6","Government Business Process Review","business process reviews",""],[1,"18","6","Gender Pay Difference Analysis","analysis of pay differences between men and women",""],[1,"18","6","Flexible Government Working Arrangements","flexible working hours and locations",""],[1,"18","6","Government Employment Attraction Initiative","enhancing the appeal of government work to attract more applicants",""],[1,"18","6","Diverse Talent Utilization Initiative","leveraging diverse talent",""],[1,"18","6","Government Employee Growth Opportunities","providing growth opportunities for government employees",""],[1,"18","6","Government Managerial Skills Development","enhancing managerial skills",""],[1,"18","6","Flexible Government Organization and Staffing Management","pursuing flexible and focused management of the organization and staffing levels in line with the Basic Policy",""],[1,"11","1","Evidence-Based Public Spending Reform","For public finances, rigorously implementing wise spending (effective and efficient expenditure) through evidence-based policy making (EBPM)",""],[1,"13","1","Evidence-Based Public Spending Mechanism","thoroughly implementing wise spending through EBPM",""],[1,"13","1","Fiscal Expenditure Reform","undertake expenditure reforms to ensure fiscal credibility",""]],"4":[[1,"7","4","Business Digitalization Support Initiative","the government ... will support initiatives such as digitalization",""],[1,"7","4","Business Automation Investment Support","investment in automation",""],[1,"7","4","SME Equipment Investment Support","support SMEs in their initiatives to invest in equipment",""],[1,"7","4","SME Market Expansion Support","support SMEs in their initiatives to ... expand their markets",""],[1,"15","4","Automation and Labor-Saving Investment Support","the government will strive to increase labor productivity by supporting automation and labor-saving investments",""],[1,"15","4","Business Succession and M&A Environment Improvement","by improving the environment for business succession and M&A",""],[1,"19","2","SME Data Management and Utilization Practices Investigation","the government will investigate the actual practices of such data management and utilization efforts in Japan and overseas by the end of the FY 2024",""],[1,"19","4","Leading Medium Enterprises and SME Earning Power Strengthening Initiative","the government will strengthen the earning power of Leading Medium Enterprises (LMEs）, the driving force behind regional economies, and SMEs, which account for 70% of employment.",""],[1,"20","2","Automation and Labor-Saving Technology Investment Support","The government will provide concentrated support for investment in automation and other labor-saving technologies.",""],[1,"20","3","Catalog-Based Labor-Saving Investment Support","The government will provide a range of industries with catalog-type support for labor-saving investments, which are simple and produce immediate effects.",""],[1,"20","3","Customized Labor-Saving Initiatives for Businesses","We will also promote customized labor-saving initiatives relevant to the operations of individual business operators.",""],[1,"20","3","Early Implementation and Operational Improvement of Support Programs","Through the process, we will implement on early implementation and operational improvements of existing support programs.",""],[1,"20","4","Sectoral Automation Action Plans","The government urges industry associations in sectors such as transportation, accommodation, food service, and other industries experiencing acute labor shortage concerns to develop autonomous action plans for the wider use of AI, robotics, and other automation technologies.",""],[1,"20","4","Sector-Focused Robot Development Promotion","We will promote the development of robots that can be easily adopted in these sectors, focusing on both hardware and software.",""],[1,"20","9","SME Support Matching Platform","the government will begin operating a matching platform that consolidates corporate information and their support needs within fiscal year ending March 31, 2024.",""],[1,"20","10","Restoration of Financial Support Measures","Financial support measures will be returned to pre-COVID-19 pandemic levels",""],[1,"21","1","Financial Support for Cost-Impacted Businesses","Additionally, financial support will continue for businesses impacted by the price surges in material costs due to the depreciation of the yen, etc.",""],[1,"21","1","SME Management Improvement and Revitalization Support","The focus of support will be placed on promoting the use of capital subordinated loans15 and initiatives for management improvement, business revitalization, and re-challenging, through assistance such as provided by Small and Medium Enterprise Vitalization Support Centers for the formulation of revitalization plans.",""],[1,"21","1","Subordinated Loan and Equity Growth Financing","The government will promote the use of subordinated loans provided by government-affiliated financial institutions and funds invested by the Organization for Small & Medium Enterprises and Regional Innovation to incorporate so-called equity into growth support.",""],[1,"21","2","Collateral-Free Corporate Financing Framework","The government will facilitate corporate financing that does not rely on real estate collateral or personal guarantees.",""],[1,"21","3","Business Succession and M&A Enabling Environment","The government will work to create an environment conducive to business succession and M&A activities.",""],[1,"21","3","Post-Merger Integration and Capital Investment Support","To promote business growth following M&A transactions, the government will implement measures to encourage companies that have engaged in M&A to undertake post-merger integration(PMI) 17 and make capital investments.",""],[1,"21","3","Business Owner Debt Guarantee Removal Support","To address this issue, the government will encourage financial institutions to propose measures enabling the removal of these guarantees when consulting with small and medium-sized enterprises regarding business succession and M&A.",""],[1,"21","3","SME Management Education and Successor Development","The government will focus on promoting management education for SME owners and fostering the development of business successors.",""],[1,"21","4","COVID-19 Hybrid Subordinated Loan","COVID-19 Hybrid Subordinated Loans, provided by Japan Finance Corporation and the Okinawa Development Finance Corporation.",""],[1,"22","1","LME and SME Growth and Quality Jobs Promotion","The government will encourage LMEs and SMEs to aim for autonomous growth and to create quality jobs.",""],[1,"22","1","Enterprise Capital Investment and Consolidation Promotion","Simultaneously, we will encourage these enterprises to make capital investments, engage in M&A and form corporate groups, etc.",""],[1,"22","2","Revision of the Basic Plan for Small Enterprise Promotion","The government will revise the Basic Plan for Small Enterprise Promotion18 by FY 2024, aiming to enhance broad-area collaboration among Commercial and Industrial Associations and Chambers of Commerce and Industry, and make other necessary modifications to foster the sustainable development of small enterprises.",""],[1,"23","1","Collaborative Sales Channel Development for SMEs","LMEs and SMEs, to develop sales channels for these enterprises through collaboration.",""]],"5":[[1,"23","2","Digital Technology and Data-Driven Society Initiative","The government will work on implementing digital technologies in the society to create new value and services and building a data-driven society by using data accumulated through DX, aiming to ensure that every citizen can enjoy its benefit.",""],[1,"23","3","Public Basic Information Database Development and Use","developing and promoting the use of a Public Basic Information Database20",""],[1,"23","3","Common Business Authentication System Adoption","expanding the adoption of the common authentication system for businesses21",""],[1,"23","4","Cross-Industry Data Sharing and Systems Linkage Platform","The government will promote the building a platform for data sharing and system linkage across the borders between enterprises and industries (Ouranos Ecosystem)",""],[1,"23","5","Quasi-Zenith Satellite Development","the government will further advance the development of quasi-zenith satellites",""],[1,"23","5","Satellite Data Utilization Initiative","the government will further advance ... the use of satellite data",""],[1,"23","6","Cross-Border Data Transfer Transparency Reform","promoting related projects, including the transparency of national systems regarding cross-border data transfers",""],[1,"23","6","Cross-Border Data Technology Verification Project","promoting related projects, including ... verifying the necessary technologies",""],[1,"23","9","Base Registry Development","Its development will enhance convenience for citizens and improve administrative efficiency.",""],[1,"25","2","Digital Administration Promotion","the entire government, centered around the Digital Agency, will promote the digitization of administration based on the Priority Policy Program28 and other initiatives.","Digital Agency"],[1,"25","2","Digitalization Review in Legislation","we will also strengthen the review of digitalization in legislation to ensure that no new analog-based regulations are introduced.","Digital Agency"],[1,"25","3","Common Digital Infrastructure Development","The government will strengthen and accelerate the development of a common digital infrastructure, which is essential for building a fully digital society.",""],[1,"25","3","Inclusive Digital Society Environment","This includes creating an environment where no one left behind29",""],[1,"25","3","Digital Talent Cultivation and Training","ensuring the cultivation and training of digital talent",""],[1,"25","3","Digitalization Monitoring and Continuous Improvement Mechanism","we will monitor various aspects related to digitalization, reference these findings in our efforts, publicly disclose information, and continuously improve.",""],[1,"25","4","My Number Card Access Facilitation Initiative","The government will work to create an environment where citizens can obtain My Number Cards without trouble",""],[1,"25","4","My Number Card Smartphone Integration","efforts will be made to enable card functions to be integrated into smartphones, thereby simplifying online procedures such as income tax filings, change of address notifications, and bank account openings",""],[1,"25","4","My Number Card Driver's License Integration","we will enhance the convenience and functionality of the Card through measures such as integration with driver's licenses",""],[1,"25","4","Public and Private My Number Card Service Expansion","Efforts will also be made to expand the use of the Card across both public and private services",""],[1,"25","4","My Number Card Emergency Services Programme","programs that utilize the Card to expedite and streamline emergency services will be promoted nationwide",""],[1,"25","5","Integrated Digital Government Procedures","Additionally, the government will enhance the integration of data required for various procedures, including tax and social security, through measures such as the use of the Mynaportal, to promote increased convenience for citizens and improved administrative efficiency30.",""],[1,"25","6","Digital Services Environment and Infrastructure Development","the development of environments and infrastructure for utilizing digital services",""],[1,"25","6","Digital Literacy Enhancement Programme","enhancement of digital literacy",""],[1,"25","6","Comprehensive Digital Accessibility Initiative","ensuring comprehensive accessibility",""],[1,"25","6","Family Register Phonetic Reading Reform","the addition and notarization of phonetic readings in family registers, primarily aimed at simplifying name search processes in databases",""],[1,"26","1","Public Sector Digital Governance Modernization","The government will work on strengthening digital governance by promoting the commonality and modernization of public sector systems, including the unification and standardization of core systems for local public entities and the establishment of data integration infrastructure in quasi-public sectors, as well as thorough utilization of software as a service (SaaS).",""]],"6":[[1,"26","3","Healthcare and Long-Term Care Workforce Development","The government will secure healthcare and long-term care workers",""],[1,"26","3","Healthcare and Long-Term Care Efficiency System","establish a system to provide higher-quality and more efficient healthcare and long-term care",""],[1,"26","3","Healthcare and Long-Term Care Digital Transformation","we will work cohesively to advance the digital transformation (DX) of healthcare and long-term care in a reliable and steady manner and provide the necessary support",""],[1,"26","3","My Number Health Insurance Card Transition","The government will promote the use of My Number Cards as health insurance cards",""],[1,"26","3","National Medical Information Platform","The government will build the National Medical Information Platform based on the Roadmap for Promoting Medical DX31",""],[1,"26","3","Electronic Medical Records Expansion","the government will strongly advance the introduction of electronic medical records",""],[1,"26","3","Electronic Medical Record Information Standardization","the standardization of electronic medical record information",""],[1,"26","3","Digital Medical Fee Revision System","the DX of medical fee revisions",""],[1,"26","3","Personal Health Record Development and Expansion","the development and expansion of Personal Health Record (PHR)",""],[1,"26","3","Secondary Use of Healthcare Information","The government will create an environment that promotes the secondary use of information shared on the National Platform for the development of new medical technologies and drug discovery",""],[1,"26","3","Public Healthcare and Long-Term Care Data Utilization","will encourage the utilization of data from public healthcare and long-term care databases",""],[1,"26","3","Healthcare Data Research Infrastructure","we will build infrastructure that allows researchers and companies to safely and efficiently utilize high-quality data",""],[1,"26","3","Healthcare DX System Management","The development and operation of systems related to healthcare DX will be primarily managed by the Health Insurance Claims Review & Reimbursement services",""],[1,"26","3","Health Insurance Claims Institution Governance Structure","the government will establish the necessary structure to fulfill this responsibility",""],[1,"26","3","Health Insurance Claims Institution Reorganization","we will fundamentally reorganize the institution into an organization capable of making quick and flexible decisions in response to advancements in information and communication technology",""],[1,"26","3","Medical Expense Adjustment Structure","work on establishing the necessary structures and strengthening efforts to adjust medical expenses to an appropriate level",""],[1,"26","3","Legal Framework for Healthcare DX","We will enact the necessary legal arrangements to advance healthcare and long-term care DX",""],[1,"27","1","AI Hospitals Social Implementation","the government will promote the social implementation of AI hospitals",""],[1,"27","1","Medical Institution Cybersecurity Measures","steadily implement cybersecurity measures in medical institutions",""],[1,"27","1","Nationwide Electronic Prescription Expansion","The government will further promote the nationwide expansion of electronic prescriptions.",""],[1,"27","1","DX Policy Programme Effectiveness Assessment","the government will collect data on the implementation of these DX-related policy programs and assess their effectiveness",""]],"7":[[1,"27","2","GIGA School Education DX Programme","Focusing on the GIGA School Program, which have been promoted as a national policy, the government will accelerate education DX by leveraging cloud environments and generative AI to further enhance children's learning and reduce the workload of teachers.",""],[1,"27","2","Joint Procurement for School Device Replacement","steady device replacements under a joint procurement scheme",""],[1,"27","2","School Communication Network Assessment and Improvement","thorough network assessments and subsequent improvements to communication networks based on these assessments",""],[1,"27","2","Regional ICT Follow-Up and Operational Support","strengthening follow-up support, including the creation of best practices to address regional disparities and broad ICT operational assistance",""],[1,"27","2","Digital Textbook and Educational Software Promotion","promoting the use of digital textbooks and other educational software",""],[1,"27","2","Teacher and Student Digital Capability Development","We will work to enhance teachers' instructional capabilities and students' information utilization skills",""],[1,"27","2","Educational Information Security and Data Protection","strengthening educational information security and personal data protection",""],[1,"27","2","Educational Data Collection and Utilization Mechanism","we will promote the collection, analysis, and utilization of educational data",""],[1,"27","2","Personalized Learning and School Work Digital Transformation","we will accelerate efforts toward personalized and self-regulated learning and advancing school work DX, including the digitalization of admission procedures and high school entrance exam processes",""],[1,"27","2","Education DX Pilot and Scaling Mechanism","Through these policies, we will create pilot cases expand them more broadly.",""],[1,"20","5","Administrative Support for Teachers","providing support for administrative and management tasks for teachers",""],[1,"27","1","Child Policy Digital Transformation Programme","the government will advance Child Policy DX in the field of childcare support, including childcare-related services, searching for daycare centers, and maternal and child health",""]],"8":[[1,"27","4","Local Transportation Digital Mobility Initiatives","The government will promote initiatives such as mobility as a service (MaaS), AI on-demand transportation, ride-hailing apps, and cashless transactions to enhance the convenience and productivity of local transportation.",""],[1,"27","4","eVTOL Regulatory Environment","We are also establishing environment such as regulations to expand the operation of eVTOLs（electric Vertical Take-Off and Landing）.",""],[1,"27","5","Flexible Highway Toll Pricing Mechanism","To alleviate highway congestion and promote regional revitalization, the government will take measures to transition the highway toll system to a flexible pricing mechanism that adjusts fees based on congestion levels, starting in FY 2025.",""],[1,"28","1","Reduced-Fee ETC Toll System Introduction","To begin with, the government will start examining the introduction of a toll system that could reduce fees by up to 50% under the current scheme32, aiming to commence this process by August.",""],[1,"28","2","Connected Autonomous Vehicle and Urban Aircraft Corridors","the government will accelerate the societal implementation of CAV(Connected Autonomous Vehicles) corridors34, equipped with priority lanes for automated driving, UAS(Urban Aircraft System) corridors.",""],[1,"28","2","Nationwide Automated Driving Implementation","In FY 2024, the government will plan and implement automated driving on general roads at approximately 100 locations.",""],[1,"28","2","Automated Driving Accident Investigation System","including establishing a specialized accident investigation system for automated driving.",""],[1,"28","3","Double-Trailer Truck Designated Route Expansion","the government will promote the expansion of designated routes for double-trailer trucks",""],[1,"28","3","Automated Driving Truck Deployment","the implementation of automated driving trucks",""],[1,"28","3","Automated Delivery Robot Deployment","automated delivery robots",""],[1,"28","3","Automated Warehouse Deployment","automated warehouses",""],[1,"28","3","Logistics Procedure Digitization","the digitization of various procedures",""],[1,"28","3","Autoflow Road Development and Social Experiment Programme","To fundamentally resolve the logistics crisis, the government will formulate a basic framework for Autoflow Road this summer, including selecting specific assumed routes, with in mind on the Tokyo-Osaka route, Japan's largest artery, and preparate for social experiments will begin promptly, aiming to realize Autoflow Road on advance routes in ten years.",""],[1,"28","3","Maritime Autonomous Surface Ship Commercialization","The government also aims to realize commercial operation of maritime autonomous surface ships by or around 2030.",""],[1,"28","6","Advanced Cruise-Assist Highway System Social Experiment","From the fiscal year 2024, a social experiment using the Advanced Cruise-Assist Highway System (AHS) will be conducted on highways, aiming to establish a main network from Tohoku to Kyushu within ten years.",""],[1,"29","2","Foreign Visitor IC Card Mobile Integration","The government will promote the integration of IC cards for foreign visitors to Japan into mobile devices",""],[1,"29","2","Multilingual Transportation and Payment App Support","the multilingual support of transportation and payment apps",""],[1,"29","2","Region-Wide Cashless and Digital Travel Systems","we will advance cross-comprehensive DX through the development of region-wide cashless systems, apps, booking sites, and data integration",""],[1,"29","2","Airport Operations Digital Transformation","The government will also advance DX in airport operations, including the streamlining of passenger procedures using new technologies such as facial recognition",""],[1,"29","2","Integrated Immigration Control Data System","will work towards strict and smooth immigration control through data integration among relevant agencies",""]],"9":[[1,"28","5","Integrated Disaster Management Information System","the government will promote the development and utilization of a disaster digital platform and data integration infrastructure centered around a new Integrated Disaster Management Information System.",""],[1,"29","6","Standardization for Disaster Victim Support Systems","For example, effective methods such as standardization to expand the adoption of systems useful for disaster victim support will be considered.",""],[1,"24","2","Emergency Intercarrier Roaming Mechanism","achieving intercarrier roaming during emergencies such as communication disruptions",""]],"10":[[1,"12","2","Energy Self-Sufficiency Improvement","by significantly improving the energy self-sufficiency rate, we will ensure energy security",""],[1,"12","2","Energy Structure Transformation for Decarbonization","By transforming the energy structure, we will seek to achieve both decarbonization and cost reduction",""],[1,"29","4","Energy-Efficient Equipment Investment Support","the government will advance support for energy-efficient equipment investments",""],[1,"29","4","ZEH and ZEB Energy Efficiency Promotion","the promotion of ZEH & ZEB36, insulation windows, and high-efficiency water heaters",""],[1,"29","4","SME Energy Efficiency Diagnostics Support System","the establishment of a support system in collaboration with local financial institutions or other to encourage SMEs to use energy efficiency diagnostics",""],[1,"29","4","Corporate Energy Conservation Disclosure System","We will also consider systems to encourage companies to disclose their energy conservation efforts",""],[1,"29","4","Household Energy Savings and Non-Fossil Fuel Promotion","to promote energy savings, conversion to non-fossil fuels, and DR37 among households",""],[1,"29","5","Renewable Energy Expansion Policy","the government will work towards its maximum expansion, ensuring that its growth takes place in a way that coexists with the local community",""],[1,"30","1","Innovative Energy Technology Development Support","develop support measures and institutional arrangements to facilitate the early development and social implementation of innovative technologies",""],[1,"30","1","International Energy Research and Standards Frameworks","establish international research and development frameworks and international standards",""],[1,"30","1","Energy Technology Skills and Supply Chain Development","support human resource development and the building a supply chain",""],[1,"30","1","Geothermal Power Development and Expansion","support the development of geothermal power and aim to expand its utilization",""],[1,"30","1","Nationwide Inter-Regional Power Grid Development","the government will advance the development of inter-regional power grids nationwide",""],[1,"30","1","Hokkaido-Honshu Submarine Transmission Project","the submarine direct current transmission between Hokkaido and Honshu is expected to be completed by FY 2030",""],[1,"30","1","Grid Flexibility and Storage Battery Deployment","we will work on securing grid flexibility and reducing curtailment through the introduction of storage batteries",""],[1,"30","1","Domestic Storage Battery Production and Technology Development","support the expansion of domestic production bases for storage batteries and the development of next-generation battery technologies",""]],"11":[[1,"30","2","Nuclear Reactor Restart Programme","The government will advance the restart of nuclear reactors with the utmost priority on safety and with the understanding of local communities based on the reviews and inspections conducted by the Nuclear Regulation Authority.",""],[1,"30","2","Next-Generation Innovative Reactor Development","We will work on the development and construction of next-generation innovative reactors that incorporate new safety mechanisms.",""],[1,"30","2","Nuclear Plant Replacement Planning","The government will formulate concrete plans to replace nuclear power plants scheduled for decommissioning with new ones on the same sites, prioritizing the understanding of local communities.",""],[1,"30","2","Nuclear Sector Investment and Capability Support","With the primary aim of improving safety, the government will promote investment and expand support for research and development, human resource development, and the maintenance and strengthening of supply chains.",""],[1,"30","2","Nuclear Fuel Cycle Promotion","The government will promote the nuclear fuel cycle",""],[1,"30","2","Nuclear Power Plant Decommissioning","advance the decommissioning of nuclear power plants in a steady and efficient manner",""],[1,"30","2","Final Disposal Public Engagement Mechanism","take the lead in fostering public understanding and actively engage with local governments to achieve final disposal",""],[1,"30","2","Nuclear Disaster Prevention and Evacuation Infrastructure","The government will enhance the nuclear disaster prevention system, including securing evacuation routes through road development.",""]],"12":[[1,"30","3","Domestic and International Hydrogen Supply Chain Development","the government will advance the development of domestic and international supply chains",""],[1,"30","3","Domestic Hydrogen Hub Establishment Support","support the establishment of domestic hubs",""],[1,"30","3","Hydrogen Technology Development Support","support ... technological development",""],[1,"30","3","Hydrogen Use Expansion Promotion System","explore the development of systems to promote the expansion of use in the electricity, gas, fuel, manufacturing, and transportation",""],[1,"31","1","Electrified Vehicle and Construction Machinery Deployment Support","In addition to promoting the introduction of electrified vehicles and electrified construction machinery",""],[1,"31","1","Commercial Fuel Cell Vehicle and Hydrogen Infrastructure Support","we will also provide intensive support for commercial vehicles such as fuel cell trucks and commercial vehicle stations, and support for hydrogen supply.",""],[1,"31","1","Non-Fossil Energy Vehicle Commercial Fleet Target Expansion","The government will consider expanding targets related to the ownership and use of non-fossil energy vehicles among commercial vehicles.",""],[1,"31","1","Carbon Recycling Fuel Research and Investment Programme","we will, through public-private collaboration, promote research, development, and capital investment in carbon recycling fuels, such as synthetic fuels (e-fuel), synthetic methane (e-methane), and domestically produced sustainable aviation fuels (SAF)",""],[1,"31","1","Industrial Fuel Transition Support for Decarbonization","Supporting their smooth transition to decarbonization, the government will first help manufacturers shift from coal and oil to natural gas, a fuel with lower CO2 emissions, and then encourage them to use low-carbon hydrogen, etc. and other alternatives in the future.",""],[1,"31","1","Carbon Dioxide Storage Commercialization Programme","We will support the commercialization of carbon dioxide storage in accordance with the CCS Business Act",""],[1,"31","1","Forest Carbon Sink Measures","implement measures for forest carbon sinks",""],[1,"30","4","Offshore Construction Capacity and Process Optimization Programme","developing the capacity of manufacturing, installation, and maintenance, as well as optimizing the entire offshore construction process through public-private collaboration.",""]],"13":[[1,"29","3","Circular Economy Development","The government will work towards realizing a circular economy.",""],[1,"31","2","Circular Economy Regulatory Review","the government is reviewing the regulations",""],[1,"31","2","Recycled Materials Financial Support Mechanism","providing financial support, which promotes the collaboration between arterial and veinous industries",""],[1,"31","2","Circular Economy Product Roadmap Support","We will also support the formulation of medium- to long-term roadmaps for individual products and materials through industry-government-academia collaboration",""],[1,"31","2","International Resource Circulation Cooperation","advance international cooperation and the establishment of international rules related to resource circulation",""],[1,"31","2","Solar Panel Disposal and Recycling Arrangements","We will also consider institutional arrangements for the disposal and recycling of solar panels and other materials",""],[1,"31","2","Plastics and Metals Recycling Technology Investment","support the development of technologies and capital investments aimed at recycling plastics and metals, such as PET bottles",""],[1,"31","2","Biomanufacturing Technology and Facilities Development","promote the development of biomanufacturing technologies and the establishment of related facilities",""],[1,"31","4","Blue Infrastructure Conservation and Restoration Initiative","Including the utilization of the J-Credit and blue carbon (carbon derived from carbon dioxide sequestrated by marine ecosystems) through the conservation, restoration, and creation of blue infrastructure (seagrass beds, tidal flats, etc., and bio-symbiotic port structures).",""],[1,"31","4","Cross-Sectoral Waste Management and Recycling Collaboration","Collaboration between manufacturing and retail sectors and waste management and recycling industries.",""],[1,"32","2","Decokatsu and 3Rs Lifestyle Transformation Campaign","We will promote “Decokatsu”50 and the 3Rs51, movements aimed at transforming people's lifestyles.",""]],"14":[[1,"32","3","Service Station Management and Network Support Programme","To ensure a stable fuel supply system, the government will provide support to service station operators, including assistance with strengthening their management capabilities and maintaining their networks.",""],[1,"32","4","Emergency Fuel Oil Price Mitigation Measure","the government initiated an emergency measure in January 2022 to mitigate the impact of volatile fuel oil prices",""],[1,"32","4","Fuel Price Volatility Risk Monitoring and Exit Planning","The government will carefully monitor risks related to price volatility, including those arising from heightened tensions in the Middle East, as well as other economic conditions.",""],[1,"33","2","Thorough Energy Conservation Programme","the government will promote thorough energy conservation",""],[1,"33","2","Renewable Energy and Nuclear Power Expansion","we will make the most of renewable energy and nuclear power, which significantly contribute to improving self-sufficiency and decarbonization",""],[1,"33","2","International Resource Diplomacy","we will advance resource diplomacy, including coordination with like-minded countries",""],[1,"33","2","Overseas Upstream Resource Development","strengthen supply chains through upstream development abroad",""],[1,"33","2","Strategic Buffer LNG Security","The government will strategically secure buffer LNG",""],[1,"33","2","Domestic Marine Resource Technology Development","we will work on developing technologies related to methane hydrates, seafloor hydrothermal deposits, and rare earth muds, among others",""],[1,"33","6","Resilient and Inclusive Supply-Chain Enhancement Initiative","Includes promotion of the Resilient and Inclusive Supply-chain Enhancement (RISE), an initiative launched under Japan's leadership in October 2023 to strengthen the resilience of supply chains for clean energy products.",""]],"15":[[1,"33","4","Next-Generation Space Technology Development Programme","the government, through public-private collaboration, will support the development and demonstration of next-generation technologies",""],[1,"33","4","Satellite Data Utilization and Constellation Development","promote the utilization of satellite data towards the constructing constellations of optical and small synthetic aperture radar satellites and optical communication satellites, etc.",""],[1,"33","4","Core Rocket Advancement Initiative","We will work on advancing core rockets",""],[1,"33","4","Space Launch Frequency Expansion","increasing launch frequency",""],[1,"33","4","Private-Sector Rocket Development Support","supporting rocket development by private companies",""],[1,"33","5","Artemis Pressurized Rover Development Project","we will commence full-scale work on the development of a pressurized rover toward the landing on the moon by a Japanese astronaut as the first non-American.",""],[1,"33","5","Beyond-Moon and Mars Exploration Research and Development","We will advance research and development for exploration beyond the moon and Mars.",""],[1,"33","5","Quasi-Zenith Satellite System Expansion","We will steadily develop the seven-satellite configuration of the Quasi-Zenith Satellite System",""],[1,"34","1","11-Satellite Configuration Study and Development","study and development towards an 11-satellite configuration",""],[1,"34","1","Space Strategy Fund Support","The government will aim to promptly provide approximately 1 trillion yen in support of the Space Strategy Fund",""],[1,"34","1","Government Space Procurement Expansion","will promote medium- to long-term government procurement to facilitate the business expansion of private companies",""],[1,"34","1","Space Transport Regulatory Framework Revision","the government, while considering potential amendments to the Act on Launching of Spacecraft, etc. and Control of Spacecraft59, will finalize the principles for necessary revisions to the current arrangements within the FY 2024",""],[1,"34","1","Space Utilization Review Coordination System","We will establish a system to enable smooth review processes in response to the global expansion of space utilization, with the Outer Space Development Strategy Headquarters serving as the control tower.",""]],"16":[[1,"34","2","Multi-Year Ocean Technology Budgeting Mechanism","the government will secure multi-year sufficient budgets across ministries",""],[1,"34","2","New Technology Commercialization and International Expansion","promote the social implementation, industrialization, and international expansion of new technologies",""],[1,"34","2","Autonomous Underwater Vehicle Research and Verification Programme","strongly promote, with predictability in supporting the research and development(R&D) of, Autonomous Underwater Vehicles and verification of their use including linkage with the Quasi-Zenith Satellite System",""],[1,"34","2","Maritime Information Industrial-Use Business Platform","building an MSIL (the MDA Situational Indication Linkages) Business Platform for the industrial use of maritime information",""],[1,"34","2","Minamitorishima Rare Earth Production Research","conducting R&D for rare earth production in the waters around Minamitorishima Island",""],[1,"34","2","Marine Jurisdiction Topographic Mapping System","developing a topographic mapping system for preservation of the sea area under the jurisdiction of",""],[1,"34","2","Mirai II Arctic Research Vessel","building Mirai II, the Arctic Research Vessel(ARV)",""],[1,"34","2","Ocean Policy Command and Coordination System","The government will establish a robust system to strengthen the command function of ocean policy",""]],"17":[[1,"34","3","Public-Private Investment for Science and Innovation","implementing measures for bold investment through public-private collaboration",""],[1,"34","3","Standards-Based Research Commercialization Mechanism","accelerating the social implementation of research and development outcomes by promoting the strategic utilization of standards",""],[1,"34","3","Cross-Disciplinary Fusion and Quantum Innovation Development","we will vigorously promote research and development, industrialization, and human resource development from a cross-disciplinary perspective in fields like fusion energy and quantum",""],[1,"35","1","International Rule-Making for Emerging Technologies","we will enhance global collaboration, leading and participating in the creation of international rules such as international standards aimed at market creation",""],[1,"35","1","International Joint Research and Human Resource Exchange","promoting international joint research and human resource exchange with like-minded countries, including the G7, as well as the Global South, including ASEAN and India",""],[1,"35","1","Next Science Technology and Innovation Basic Plan","the government will start discussions within this year on the next Science, Technology, and Innovation Basic Plan",""],[1,"35","2","Universities for International Research Excellence Programme","The government will steadily advance efforts towards the sustainable creation of innovation through the Universities for International Research Excellence program by realizing world-class research universities and strengthening the functions of \"core regional\" and/or \"distinctive\" research universities.",""],[1,"35","2","National Research and Development Agency Capability Enhancement","Specifically, we will further strengthen these agencies' capabilities in securing and developing talent for the early social implementation of research outcomes and for agile responses to nationally significant issues, as well as in the areas of research security and integrity.",""]],"18":[[1,"37","2","Startup Support and Network-Building Programme","Supporting startups and building their networks",""],[1,"37","3","National Startup Ecosystem Development Initiative","The government will build an ecosystem where startups are continuously created and growing, since they are the driving force behind innovation creation and productivity improvement as well as the players in solving social issues through the social implementation of new technologies.",""],[1,"37","4","Young Startup Human Resources Development Programme","the government will work to find and nurture young human resources",""],[1,"37","4","Female Entrepreneurship Support Programme","support female entrepreneurs",""],[1,"37","4","Entrepreneurship Education Enhancement Programme","enhance entrepreneurship education",""],[1,"37","4","Overseas Entrepreneur Dispatch Programme","send entrepreneurs overseas",""],[1,"37","4","Startup Overseas Expansion Support Programme","we will support them to participate in overseas exhibitions and expand to the Global South",""],[1,"37","4","Foreign Investment Attraction and Overseas Promotion Initiative","we will strengthen the dissemination of initiatives overseas",""],[1,"37","4","Rural Startup Talent Matching Initiative","we will strengthen our engagement in matching local companies with human resources from metropolitan areas",""],[1,"37","4","Regional Startup Ecosystem Development Programme","creating an ecosystem of startups in each base city",""],[1,"37","4","Global Startup Campus Initiative","The government will further embody the Global Startup Campus (GSC) Initiative as the world's most advanced startup creation base",""],[1,"37","4","Global Startup Campus Research and Incubation Base","The flagship base will have cutting-edge research functions through organic collaboration with top universities overseas, invitation of excellent researchers, exchange programs and so on, and will also provide support in terms of incubation, intellectual property and legal affairs, etc.",""],[1,"37","4","Global Startup Network Collaboration Mechanism","The government will build a global network by strengthening collaboration between domestic and foreign startups using the said base as a hub.",""],[1,"37","5","Startup Public Procurement and Matching Mechanism","We will promote the use of a mechanism that enables discretionary contracts to meet the public administration’s procurement needs with advanced and unique new technologies that startups possess.",""],[1,"38","1","SBIR Research and Development Social Implementation System","We will promote the SBIR system 67 to promote the social implementation of research and development.",""],[1,"38","2","Startup Long-Term Purchase Commitment Support","The government will consider supporting a startup company so that it can obtain a long-term purchase commitment agreement (off-take agreement) 68 from its operating company that backs up the startup, when both companies proceed with their collaboration.",""],[1,"38","3","Deep Tech Research and Business Development Support","The government will enhance support stages, content and methods for research and business development in the deep tech field.",""],[1,"38","3","Growth-Stage Deep Tech Financing Mechanism","We will develop an environment in which funds can be smoothly supplied in accordance with the growth stages, including the later stage, by activating the distribution of unlisted shares and strengthening the investment function of public and private funds.",""],[1,"38","3","Angel Tax System Reinvestment Period Extension","The government will consider extending the reinvestment period under the Angel Tax System.",""],[1,"38","4","Startup M&A Revitalization Initiative","the government will revitalize M&A activities to diversify exit strategies.",""],[1,"38","4","Startup Open Innovation Promotion","We will promote new open innovation involving startups, in addition to universities and large corporations",""],[1,"38","4","Financial Reporting Review for Startup M&A","we will examine the state of financial reporting, including non-amortization of goodwill.",""],[1,"38","5","Business Entry, Exit, and Startup Regulatory Reform","The government will promote regulatory reforms and the protection and utilization of intellectual property from the viewpoint of facilitating the entry and exit of companies and fostering startups.",""],[1,"38","5","Majority-Vote Financial Debt Reduction Bill","In order to facilitate prompt business restructuring according to the judgment of management, we aim to swiftly submit a bill that permits the reduction of financial debts through a majority vote.",""]],"19":[[1,"36","2","Leading Asset Management Center Promotion Policy","(5) Promoting Japan as a Leading Asset Management Center",""],[1,"36","3","Asset Management Industry Reform","the government will advance reforms in the asset management industry",""],[1,"36","3","Financial and Asset Management Special Zones","we will promote the Special Zones for Financial and Asset Management Businesses by leveraging the National Strategic Special Zones system",""],[1,"36","3","Asset Owner Principles","the government will promote the reform of asset ownership by establishing Asset Owner Principles that define common principles for investment, governance, and risk management",""],[1,"36","3","Corporate Pension Asset Management Transparency","increasing visibility in the asset management of corporate pensions for subscribers",""],[1,"36","4","NISA Procedure Simplification and Utilization Reform","The government will promote further simplification and rationalization of procedures for the new NISA (Nippon Individual Savings Account) and its utilization",""],[1,"36","4","Financial and Economic Education Enhancement Programme","enhancing financial and economic education with the Japan Financial Literacy and Education Corporation (J-FLEC)",""],[1,"36","4","Customer-Oriented Financial Institution Operations","ensuring customer-oriented business operations in financial institutions",""],[1,"36","4","International Financial Center Promotion Initiative","strengthening external promotion for the realization of Japan as an international financial center in Japan through events in Japan Weeks",""],[1,"36","4","Corporate Governance and Securities Disclosure Reform","implementing corporate governance reforms, including preparing the environment for the disclosure of securities reports before shareholder meetings",""],[1,"36","4","NISA Contribution Limit Review","We will make efforts to reach a conclusion by the end of 2024 on raising the contribution limit",""],[1,"37","1","iDeCo Benefit Eligibility Age Revision","the upper limit of age eligibility to start receiving benefits for iDeCo (Individual-type Defined Contribution pension plan).",""],[1,"37","1","iDeCo Procedure Simplification","we will work to reduce the burden on participants and beneficiaries by simplifying procedures.",""],[1,"37","1","Banking and Securities Firewall Regulation Review","We will review the regulations on the firewall between banking and securities operations65.",""],[1,"37","6","Financial Group Information-Sharing and Conflict-of-Interest Regulations","These regulations prohibit banks and securities firms within a financial group from sharing customers' non-public information without the customers' consent, and from engaging in actions that create conflicts of interest.",""],[1,"38","6","Impact Investment Data and Evaluation Framework","discussions will be held at the Impact Consortium, etc., to strengthen support for social entrepreneurs (impact startups), etc., by developing data and establishing evaluation methods that will promote investment.",""],[1,"38","6","Public-Private Equity Investment Promotion","public and private institutions will work together to promote the engagement of equity investment.",""],[1,"40","3","International Financial Regulation and Supervision Discussions","In order to strengthen the financial system, Japan will contribute to international discussions on the appropriate modus of regulation and supervision at the Financial Stability Board (FSB),76 etc., as well as such discussions on how to respond to new risks.",""],[1,"40","7","International Financial System Stability Coordination Mechanism","Representatives from central banks and financial supervisory authorities of major countries and regions discuss international issues related to financial system stability, including coordination of works by standard-setting entities in the banking, securities and insurance sectors.",""]],"20":[[1,"38","7","Free and Fair Economic Zone Expansion","The government will expand a free and fair economic zone",""],[1,"38","7","Rules-Based Multilateral Trading System Strengthening","will maintain and strengthen a rules-based multilateral trading system",""],[1,"38","7","CPTPP Accession and General Review Leadership","Japan will take the lead in accession requests and the “General Review”",""],[1,"39","1","Transparent RCEP Agreement Implementation","We will work to ensure the transparent implementation of the RCEP Agreement",""],[1,"39","1","Indo-Pacific Economic Partnership Promotion","promote economic partnership in the Indo-Pacific region through IPEF",""],[1,"39","1","WTO System Strengthening","strengthen the WTO system",""],[1,"39","1","Economic Partnership Agreement Expansion","expand EPAs",""],[1,"39","2","Trade Digital Transformation Infrastructure Development","we will promote trade DX by developing domestic infrastructure such as legal revisions, utilizing trade platforms, and standardizing data.",""],[1,"39","2","Overseas Financial Support Publicity Programme","we will work on publicizing financial support measures in accordance with local circumstances",""],[1,"39","2","Overseas Diplomatic Mission Business Support","strengthening support through the use of overseas diplomatic missions",""],[1,"39","2","Multilateral Development Bank Collaborative Projects","promoting formulation of collaborative projects with local companies through cooperation with multilateral development banks",""],[1,"39","2","Overseas Infrastructure Expansion Strategy Review","reviewing the strategy for overseas expansion of infrastructure systems with a view to 2030",""],[1,"39","2","National International Standardization Strategy","formulating a new national strategy for international standardization",""],[1,"39","2","Tax Treaty Network Expansion","expanding the network of tax treaties",""],[1,"39","2","ODA Co-Creation Cooperation Initiative","Japan will work to support the overseas expansion of Japanese companies by utilizing ODA through proactive cooperation such as Co-creation for common agenda initiative70 as well as public finance",""],[1,"39","2","Third-Country Export and Industrial Cooperation Support","promote exports via third countries through industrial cooperation and establishment of base",""],[1,"39","2","Public-Private Trade Cooperation Forums","establish frameworks such as public-private forums",""],[1,"39","2","International Digital Public Infrastructure Development","build digital public infrastructure with reliable and willing countries",""],[1,"39","2","Energy Communications and Transport Project Demonstration","support the demonstration and implementation of projects in the fields of energy, communications, and transportation, etc.",""],[1,"39","2","Water Cycle and Disaster Risk Reduction Technical Cooperation","provide technical cooperation in the fields of maintenance or recovery of a sound water cycle or water-related disaster risk reduction",""],[1,"39","2","Smart City Project Formation Support","support the formation of smart city projects",""],[1,"39","2","Trade Insurance Risk Handling Capacity Strengthening","strengthen the risk handling capability of trade insurance in light of changes in the international environment",""],[1,"39","2","Low-Impact Agricultural Forestry and Fishery Technology Diffusion","diffuse agricultural, forestry, and fishery technologies 71 that both reduce the environmental load and improve productivity",""],[1,"39","2","TICAD9 Africa Support","support Africa through TICAD9",""],[1,"39","3","Support for Japanese Companies' Activities in Ukraine","Toward the reconstruction of Ukraine, Japan will support local activities of Japanese companies, including startups.",""],[1,"39","4","International University Cooperation for Skilled Human Resources","the government will secure highly skilled young foreign human resources in Southeast and South Asia by strengthening cooperation with local universities",""],[1,"39","4","Status of Residence System Improvement Measures","considering necessary measures based on the survey on improvement of the status of residence system",""],[1,"40","1","International Student Recruitment and Scholarship Initiative","promote accepting excellent international students through inviting world top-level researchers and prioritizing the allocation of scholarships to students in specific regions",""],[1,"40","1","Overseas-Domestic Corporate Collaboration and Investment Promotion","encourage collaboration between overseas and domestic companies including capital investment, etc.",""],[1,"40","1","Global Public Relations for International Initiatives","work on public relations of these initiatives around the world",""],[1,"40","1","International Initiative Follow-up Mechanism","We will follow up these initiatives.",""]],"21":[[1,"40","2","UHC Knowledge Hub Establishment","we will establish the UHC Knowledge Hub in Japan as a global hub for human resource development and knowledge gathering",""],[1,"40","2","Foreign Medical Personnel Development","develop foreign medical personnel in cooperation with ERIA",""],[1,"40","2","International Medical and Long-Term Care Expansion","expand medical and long-term care internationally, including medical inbound",""],[1,"40","2","Global Vaccine and Tuberculosis Partnership Support","contribute to the Vaccine Alliance and the Stop TB Partnership",""],[1,"40","2","Climate-Resilient Low-Carbon Healthcare Promotion","promote the efforts of the Alliance for Transformative Action on Climate Change and Health (ATACH) to build a climate change-resilient, low-carbon and sustainable healthcare system",""],[1,"40","2","Private and Impact Investment Mobilization","attract private funds, including impact investments",""],[1,"40","7","International Public-Private Tuberculosis Partnership","An international public-private partnership aimed at ending tuberculosis by 2030, with the United Nations Office for Project Services serving as the secretariat.",""]],"22":[[1,"41","5","My Number and Residence Card Integration","the government will work on integrating the My Number Card and the Residence Card",""],[1,"41","5","Accredited Japanese-Language Institute System","developing and utilizing a system of Accredited Japanese-language institutes",""],[1,"41","5","Regional Japanese-Language Education and Curriculum Development","developing systems for regional Japanese language education and education using a model curriculum for daily Japanese and education of foreign students",""],[1,"41","5","Online Learning Access for Foreign Nationals","securing online learning opportunities and etc.",""],[1,"41","5","Electronic Travel Authorization System","we will work on preparing for the introduction of an electronic system for travel authorization for smooth and strict screening as part of the Immigration DX",""],[1,"41","5","Refugee Protection and Support","protecting and supporting refugees, etc. promptly and reliably",""],[1,"41","5","Diversified Deportation Measures","solving the issue of deportation evasion through diversified deportation methods",""],[1,"41","6","Employment-for-Skill-Development Program","we will develop a necessary system, set up the expected number of acceptances each field and the targeted industrial fields",""],[1,"42","1","Stricter Licensing Criteria for Support Organizations","embody policies concerning the stricter criteria of license system for supervising and support organizations, etc.",""],[1,"42","1","Specified Skilled Worker System Optimization","With regard to the Specified Skilled Worker System, we will take appropriate measures for its optimization, including strengthening cooperation between the implementing organizations and local governments.",""],[1,"42","1","Minimum Wage and Equal Pay Compliance","Appropriate working environments shall be ensured through securing compliance with minimum wages and equal pay for equal work.",""]],"23":[[1,"45","1","Urban Revitalization Initiative","the government will work to revitalize cities",""],[1,"45","1","People-Centered Compact Green Towns Development","create people-centered, compact and green towns",""],[1,"45","1","Nature-Positive Local Activities Programme","promote local activities that aim at realizing nature positive",""],[1,"45","1","Green Infrastructure Development","encourage a green infrastructure",""],[1,"45","1","Regional Shopping Hub Development","the government will support local governments' proactive efforts, including the development of shopping hub facilities in accordance with the respective local circumstances",""],[1,"45","1","Horizontal Good-Practice Dissemination Mechanism","disseminating and deploying good practices horizontally",""],[1,"45","3","Public Park Utilization Initiative","Use of parks",""],[1,"45","3","Post Office Community Service Hubs","use of post offices as a base for consolidating and providing various services",""],[1,"45","3","Natural Capital Data and International Rules Initiative","This includes the preparation of data on natural capital, etc., the dissemination of such information, and the initiative to form international rules.",""],[1,"46","4","Disadvantaged Area Regional Development Measures","the government will promote the development of Okinawa and Hokkaido, and take measures to address areas where conditions are unfavorable, such as depopulated areas, peninsulas, remote islands, Amami, Ogasawara, and areas with heavy snowfall, etc.",""],[1,"46","4","Okinawa Entrepreneurship Support Initiative","support for entrepreneurship at the Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology Graduate University",""],[1,"46","4","Northern Okinawa and Remote Islands Settlement Improvement","improving the settlement environment in the northern part of the prefecture and remote islands",""],[1,"46","4","Futenma Site Acquisition and Airport Integration","acquiring the site of the Marine Corps Air Station Futenma in advance with a view to its return and its integral use with Naha Airport",""],[1,"46","4","Hokkaido Production Space Development","maintaining and developing Production Spaces that support food, tourism, and Zero Carbon Hokkaido",""],[1,"46","4","Hokkaido Digital Industry Integration","promoting the integration of digital industries",""],[1,"46","4","Northern Territories Neighboring Region Development","promoting the development of the Region neighboring the Northern Territories further",""],[1,"47","1","Upopoy National Ainu Museum and Park Enhancement","enhancing Upopoy National Ainu Museum and Park",""],[1,"47","2","Tax Incentives for Rural Enterprise Relocation","the use of the tax system to strengthen local bases",""],[1,"47","2","Community-Based Enterprise Development","the establishment of community-based enterprises through industry-academic-government-financial cooperation",""],[1,"47","2","Local Human Resources Securing Initiative","efforts to secure local human resources, such as Local Vitalization Cooperators93",""],[1,"47","2","Rural Infrastructure and Coworking Space Development","The government will develop infrastructure and other facilities94, including coworking spaces to expand the population with strong relationship to the areas and promote diverse lifestyles such as dual habitation and multi-location life.",""],[1,"47","7","Community Revitalization Entrepreneurship and Cooperatives","This includes the use of community revitalization entrepreneurs and specific community development project cooperatives.",""],[1,"47","7","Wide-Area Regional Revitalization Infrastructure Development","This includes efforts based on the Act for Partial Revision of the Act on Infrastructure Development for Wide-Area Regional Revitalization (Act No. 31 of 2024).",""],[1,"47","7","Traditional Events and Hot Springs Branding Initiative","This includes cooperation in research and studies as well as dissemination of information by relevant organizations for branding traditional events and hot springs for their sustainability and development.",""],[1,"47","7","Mountain Hut and Trail Conservation and Long Trail Utilization","This includes the maintenance and conservation of mountain huts and trails as well as utilization of long trails.",""],[1,"47","7","Airport Operations Workforce Development","This includes promoting efforts to secure and nurture human resources in airport operations such as ground handling and security screening.",""],[1,"85","5","Wide-Area Multi-Sectoral Cooperation for Sustainable Communities","the government will promote wide-area and multi-sectoral cooperation ... in order to build sustainable local communities",""],[1,"86","2","Regional Living Areas Development Partnership","the government will work to promote the construction and development of regional living areas through wide-area, multi-sectoral, and public-private partnerships",""],[1,"86","2","Self-Reliant Regional Management Entities","the government will work to foster self-reliant regional management entities toward the circulation of regional economies",""],[1,"88","4","Regional Human Investment and Employment Creation Programme","We will also ... create new employment opportunities by investing in people at the regional level",""],[1,"88","4","Local Regional Population Flow Promotion","strengthening the flow of people to local regions",""]],"25":[[1,"49","4","Sustainable Forestry Management Legal System","The government aims to submit to the next ordinary Diet session a legal system to promote the development of management entities that can use forest resources sustainably and to promote consolidation of forestry operations.",""],[1,"49","4","Forest Roads and Infrastructure Improvement","We will move ahead with the improvement of forest roads and other infrastructure",""],[1,"49","4","Forest Reforestation Programme","We will move ahead with the improvement of forest roads and other infrastructure, reforestation, shift to domestic timber, expansion of timber use105, and measures against pollen allergy, etc.",""],[1,"49","4","Domestic Timber Use Expansion","We will move ahead with the improvement of forest roads and other infrastructure, reforestation, shift to domestic timber, expansion of timber use105, and measures against pollen allergy, etc.",""],[1,"49","4","Pollen Allergy Countermeasures","We will move ahead with the improvement of forest roads and other infrastructure, reforestation, shift to domestic timber, expansion of timber use105, and measures against pollen allergy, etc.",""],[1,"49","5","Fisheries Resource Management Programme","We will properly manage fisheries resources",""],[1,"49","5","Fisheries Operational Model Reform","convert operational forms",""],[1,"49","5","Aquaculture Industry Development Programme","make the aquaculture industry a growth industry",""],[1,"49","5","Fishery Operator Human Resources Development","nurture human resources to become fishery operators",""],[1,"49","5","Fishery Business Stabilization Support","stabilize their businesses",""],[1,"49","5","Fishing Vessel and Production Infrastructure Improvement","improve fishing vessels and other production infrastructure",""],[1,"49","5","UMIGYO Value Utilization Projects","promote UMIGYO (Projects that utilize the value and",""]],"26":[[1,"51","4","Donation Promotion Initiative","the promotion of donations",""],[1,"51","4","Support Programme for Private Social Issue-Solving Entities","the government will strengthen support for private entities working to solve social issues, including support through intermediate support organizations that support NPO projects",""],[1,"52","1","Incorporated NPO Administrative and Compliance Support","the government will put into place a proper environment to promote online administrative procedures as well as measures against the financing of terrorism",""],[1,"52","1","Public Interest Corporation and Charitable Trust System Development","the government will develop necessary systems for implementing the new system",""],[1,"52","1","Unified Information Provision Platform","as well as a unified information provision platform",""],[1,"52","1","Dormant Deposit Social Issue Organization Support","we will promote the development and self-reliance of organizations working to solve social issues via the relevant activity-support organizations",""],[1,"52","1","Dormant Deposit Social Investment Projects","through smooth implementation of the related investment projects",""],[1,"52","1","Pay For Success and Social Impact Bond Expansion","The government will work to further expand the use of the Pay For Success contracting system (PFS), including the Social Impact Bond (SIB)",""],[1,"52","1","Hometown Tax Donation System Review","we will comprehensively examine the status of our engagement to date, and consider how the system should be implemented in the future",""]],"27":[[1,"52","3","Women’s Recruitment, Development, and Promotion Programme","the government will strengthen the recruitment, development, and promotion of women so as to achieve the numerical targets for female executives of companies listed on the Prime Market",""],[1,"52","3","Female Entrepreneurship Support Programme","support female entrepreneurs",""],[1,"52","3","Women’s Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","promote reskilling and upskilling such as raising women’s income and helping women get employed in the digital sector",""],[1,"52","3","Work-Life Balance Support through Investor Evaluations","support their balancing of work with childcare, long-term care, and health issues through the use of investor evaluations",""],[1,"52","3","Women’s Empowerment and Unconscious Bias Awareness Initiative","raise awareness to promote women’s empowerment, including the elimination of the effect of unconscious bias",""],[1,"52","3","Women’s Advancement in Public Service Programme","promote women’s further advancement in the public service sector",""],[1,"52","3","Regional Gender Equality Core Organizations","promote the formation of a gender-equal society at the regional level through the examination and elaboration of new core organizations",""],[1,"52","3","Industry-Academia-Government STEM Participation Initiative for Girls","the government will promote joint efforts by industry, academia, government, and communities to foster the interest of female junior and senior high school students and expand their motivation and abilities",""],[1,"53","1","Gender-Responsive Disaster Prevention and Reconstruction","The government will work on advancing disaster prevention and reconstruction from the perspective of gender equality",""],[1,"53","1","Women, Peace and Security Agenda","the promotion of women, peace and security (WPS117)agenda",""],[1,"53","1","Sexual and Domestic Violence Victim Support Measures","the promotion of measures against sexual crimes, sexual violence, and domestic violence, including enhancing consultation and support for various victims118",""],[1,"53","1","Support Systems for Women Facing Difficulties","the strengthening of support for women with difficult problems by steadily implementing laws on support for them, such as establishing public-private collaboration-type support systems",""],[1,"53","1","Measures Against Malicious Host Clubs","the promotion of measures against malicious “host clubs”",""],[1,"53","1","Gender-Responsive Workplace and Community Consultation Support","the enhancement of consultation support systems in workplaces and communities based on gender differences",""],[1,"53","1","FemTech Promotion Initiative","the promotion of FemTech",""],[1,"53","1","Lifelong Women's Health Services and Research","the support for lifelong women's health, such as the enhancement of medical services and research at the (provisionally named) National Center for Women's Health",""],[1,"53","2","Women's Participation in Policymaking","the government will promote the participation of women in the policymaking process.",""],[1,"53","2","Sex-Disaggregated Policy Analysis and Data Collection","In planning and implementing policies and projects, we will consider sex-disaggregated differences in the impact and needs, and will strengthen necessary sex-disaggregated data collection and analysis.",""],[1,"54","4","Workplace Harassment Prevention Measures","The government will strengthen measures against harassment in the workplace, including customer harassment, with a view to considering legislation.",""]],"29":[[1,"54","3","Foods with Function Claims Reliability System","The government will work to establish a highly reliable system of Foods with Function Claims.",""],[1,"54","3","Food Loss and Waste Reduction Policy","The Basic Policy126 will be revised within FY 2024 to reduce food loss and waste, including promoting food donations.",""],[1,"54","3","Consumer Policy Basic Plan","we will formulate a new Basic Plan on Consumer Policy within FY 2024",""],[1,"54","3","Whistleblower Protection System Reform","reform of the whistleblower protection system",""],[1,"54","3","Consumer Affairs Consultation Digital Transformation","promotion of the Consumer Affairs Consultation DX",""],[1,"54","5","Pollen Source Reduction and Cedar Plantation Replanting Measures","the government will take measures against sources aiming to halve the amount of pollen produced in about 30 years, including cutting and replanting in the priority areas for cutting down Japanese cedar plantations.",""],[1,"54","6","Cedar Pollen Rice Commercialization Partnership","promotion of public-private cooperative efforts to commercialize cedar pollen rice",""],[1,"55","1","Special Heat Stroke Alert Information Use","against heat illness, such as the use of Special Heat Stroke Alert information.",""],[1,"55","2","Bear-Inflicted Damage Prevention Measures","In order to prevent injury or death caused by bears, the government will promote the prevention of infestations in people's living areas based on the Policy Package of Measures Against Bear-Inflicted Damage129.",""],[1,"55","3","Invasive Alien Species Early Detection and Rapid Response","The government will promote early detection and rapid response for long-horned beetles and the like, which have become newly regulated under the revised Invasive Alien Species Act130.",""],[1,"55","4","Post-COVID-19 Condition and Vaccine Side-Effects Research Programme","The government continues promoting investigation and research regarding post COVID-19 condition and side effects after vaccination.",""],[1,"55","5","Online Rabies Prevention Procedures","The government will promote measures against zoonotic diseases such as online procedures related to the Rabies Prevention Act.",""],[1,"55","6","PFAS Scientific Knowledge and Countermeasures Initiative","The government will enhance scientific knowledge and promote necessary countermeasures based on the Direction of Future Actions on PFAS134.",""],[1,"54","6","Vaccine and Therapeutics Research and Development","research and development of vaccines and therapeutics",""]],"30":[[1,"55","7","Public-Private Partnership Investment Promotion","The government will promote public-private partnership investment to an internationally comparable level",""],[1,"55","7","Next-Generation Creators and Artists Development","we will nurture the next generation of creators and artists",""],[1,"55","7","Cultural Activities Support Environment","develop a proper environment to promote vibrant activities",""],[1,"55","7","Cultural Facilities Function Strengthening","strengthening the functions of cultural facilities that will serve as bases",""],[1,"55","7","National Theater Redevelopment","The government will take responsibility for the urgent redevelopment of the National Theater",""],[1,"55","7","National Center for Media Arts Base Development","the government will promote the development of a base with the functions of the National Center for Media Arts (tentative name)",""],[1,"56","1","International Cultural Facilities Expansion and Dissemination","we will strengthen the relevant functions, including the global expansion of national cultural facilities, which will become international bases, such as the New National Theater",""],[1,"56","1","Digital Cultural Dissemination Initiative","strengthen the dissemination to both inside and outside of Japan by utilizing digital technologies in use at museums and art galleries, etc.",""],[1,"56","1","Integrated Cultural Property Preservation System","the government will promote the sustainable preservation and utilization of cultural properties in an integrated manner, including efforts to establish a system for ascertaining, preserving, and inheriting cultural properties",""],[1,"56","1","Public-Private Cultural Property Value Enhancement","strengthening the enhancement of added value of cultural properties through public-private partnerships",""],[1,"56","1","Japan Heritage Revitalization Programme","revitalizing Japan Heritage",""],[1,"56","1","Local Cultural and Tourism Revitalization","the government will promote local community revitalization through the promotion of food culture and other lifestyle culture, architectural culture, and cultural tourism",""],[1,"56","1","Art Market Revitalization Initiative","the revitalization of art markets",""],[1,"56","1","Japan Expo Global Cultural Expansion","the strengthening of global expansion capabilities through Japan Expo 2.0, etc.",""],[1,"56","1","Cultural Digital Transformation and Archiving","We will also promote DX, including digital archiving",""],[1,"56","1","Creator Compensation Return Mechanism","the return of compensation to creators",""],[1,"56","1","Inclusive Cultural Access Programme","secure opportunities for children and persons with disabilities to view and experience culture and arts",""],[1,"56","1","Traditional and Contemporary Culture Promotion","promote traditional performing arts, theatrical arts, Japanese cinema, and print culture, including books",""],[1,"56","1","Library-Bookstore Cooperation and Accessible Reading","promoting cooperation between bookstores and libraries and promoting barrier-free reading",""],[1,"56","1","Bookstore Activation Initiative","activate bookstores",""],[1,"56","1","Kitanomaru Garden Cultural and Science Hub","By strengthening the functions of Kitanomaru Garden, we aim to improve its attractiveness as a hub for the transmission of cutting-edge science and technology, culture and arts.",""],[1,"56","1","National Archives Expansion and Functional Strengthening","the government will promote strengthening of the functions of the National Archives of Japan with a view to opening its new annex.",""],[1,"56","3","Cultural Property Repair Workforce Support","the promotion of securing human resources, including raising the wages of repair technicians based on the artisans projects for cultural properties",""],[1,"56","3","National Cultural Properties Repair Center Development","the development of the National Cultural Properties Repair Center",""],[1,"56","3","Takamatsuzuka Tomb Mural Preservation Facility Initiative","the promotion of initiatives based on the basic plan of the Takamatsuzuka Tomb Mural Painting Preservation and Management Publicity Utilization Facility (tentative name)",""],[1,"56","3","Local Exhibitions of Imperial Collections","local exhibitions of some of the collection of the Museum of the Imperial Collections, Sannomaru Shozokan",""],[1,"56","3","Cultural Heritage Digital Archives Initiative","efforts to compile and share digital archives, as well as to promote their use",""],[1,"56","3","Theater and Music Hall Support Programme","support for theaters, music halls, etc.",""]],"31":[[1,"56","2","Martial Arts and Sports Tourism Promotion","the government will promote martial arts and sports tourism",""],[1,"56","2","Sports Hospitality Development","popularize sports hospitality",""],[1,"56","2","Stadium and Arena Development Initiative","develop and utilize stadiums and arenas",""],[1,"56","2","Community Sports Complex Development","promote sports complexes in which facilities are developed and utilized in a comprehensive and complex manner for community development",""],[1,"56","2","Sports Digital Transformation and Esports Collaboration","collaborate with sports DX and other industries, including the utilization of esports",""],[1,"56","2","Overseas Sports Sector Expansion","expand overseas",""],[1,"56","2","Advanced Technology-Based Conditioning Initiative","improve life performance through advanced technology-based conditioning",""],[1,"57","1","Disability Sports Promotion Programme","The government will promote sports for the persons with disabilities in cooperation with private companies",""],[1,"57","1","Comprehensive Local Sports Environment Enhancement","enhance the local sports environment in a comprehensive manner",""],[1,"57","1","International Sports Tournament Hosting Support","We will also support the hosting of large-scale international tournaments",""],[1,"57","6","Community Sports Promotion and Safety System","Establishing a system to promote community sports, ensuring the quantity and quality of instructors, establishing a system to ensure safety, and making effective use of school physical education facilities, etc.",""],[1,"57","6","Hosting Major International Sporting Events","2025 World Athletics Championships and Deaflympics, 2026 Asian Games and Asian Para Games, World Masters Games 2027 Kansai, etc.",""]],"32":[[1,"57","3","Diplomatic Capability Strengthening","we will further strengthen our diplomatic capabilities.",""],[1,"57","4","Japan-U.S. Alliance and Partner Cooperation","Japan will build on the Japan-U.S Alliance and work together with allies and like-minded countries in Europe, NATO, ASEAN, Pacific Island countries, and the Middle East, including Australia, India, South Korea, the United Kingdom, and the Philippines.",""],[1,"57","4","Global Rules for Food Health Climate and Plastics","The government will develop and strengthen rules on global issues such as food, health, climate change, and plastic pollution.",""],[1,"57","4","Global South Engagement through Multilateral Dialogues","We will also take opportunities such as TICAD9, PALM10142, and the Central Asia + Japan Dialogue and Summit Meeting to strengthen our engagement to the Global South, including Africa, Pacific Island countries, and Central Asia.",""],[1,"57","5","Sanctions Against Russia","The government will promote sanctions against Russia",""],[1,"57","5","Support for Ukraine and Neighboring Countries","strongly supporting143 Ukraine and neighboring countries.",""],[1,"57","6","Ukraine Reconstruction Support","To support the reconstruction of Ukraine, in addition to the five actions announced at the Japan-Ukraine Economic Reconstruction Promotion Conference, such as the conclusion of a new tax treaty",""],[1,"58","1","Private Sector Financing Mobilization through ODA","mobilizing private sector financing by using ODA as a catalyst",""],[1,"58","1","JICA Overseas Cooperation Volunteer Deployment","utilization of JICA Overseas Cooperation Volunteers",""],[1,"58","1","International Organization Cooperation","utilization of ... proven international organizations",""],[1,"58","1","NGO Cooperation for International Cooperation","cooperation with NGOs",""],[1,"58","1","Humanitarian Crisis Support","support for humanitarian crises such as the situation in Gaza",""],[1,"58","1","International Cooperation Implementation Capacity Strengthening","make necessary efforts to enhance the foundation of implementation",""],[1,"58","1","Official Security Assistance Strengthening","Japan will strategically promote and strengthen OSA",""],[1,"58","2","Nuclear Disarmament and Non-Proliferation Initiative","To achieve a world without nuclear weapons, Japan will lead international efforts for disarmament and non-proliferation, including nuclear weapons, through the steady implementation of the “Hiroshima Action Plan”.",""],[1,"58","2","United Nations and Security Council Reform","strengthening the functions of the United Nations, including Security Council reform",""],[1,"58","2","Japanese Staffing in International Organizations","increasing the number of Japanese staff in international organizations",""],[1,"58","2","International Law-Based Dispute Resolution","resolving disputes based on international law, including through international judicial proceedings",""],[1,"58","2","Women, Peace and Security and Human Security Action","We will also work on issues such as strengthening the functions of the United Nations, including Security Council reform, increasing the number of Japanese staff in international organizations, resolving disputes based on international law, including through international judicial proceedings, WPS146, and human security.",""],[1,"58","2","Japan Affinity and Knowledge Network Expansion","We will also strive for expanding the circle of people with a great affinity toward or knowledge of Japan, including people of Japanese descent.",""],[1,"58","2","International Information Dissemination on Japan","as well as to disseminate information about Japan’s territory, sovereignty, and others, to both inside and outside of Japan.",""],[1,"58","3","Japan–North Korea Relations Normalization Policy","The government aims to normalize its relations with North Korea, in accordance with the Japan-DPRK Pyongyang Declaration, through comprehensively resolving outstanding issues of concern such as the abductions147, nuclear, and missile issues, as well as settlement of the unfortunate past.",""],[1,"58","4","Foreign and Consular Policy Implementation Structure Strengthening","the government will fundamentally strengthen the foreign and consular policy implementation structure",""],[1,"58","4","Diplomatic Personnel System Strengthening","we will strengthen personnel systems",""],[1,"58","4","Diplomatic Financial Base Development","develop financial bases that form the basis of diplomacy",""],[1,"58","4","Diplomatic Mission Resilience and Emergency Protection System","enhance the resilience of diplomatic missions, including the system to protect Japanese nationals in emergencies",""],[1,"58","4","Consular Services Improvement","improve consular services",""],[1,"58","4","Diplomatic Digitalization and Information Protection Enhancement","enhance digitalization and information protection",""],[1,"58","5","International Anti-Corruption Measures","Japan will implement anti-corruption measures in cooperation with the G7 and international organizations.",""],[1,"58","5","JICA Human Resource Development Cooperation","Includes cooperation in human resource development by JICA",""]],"33":[[1,"59","1","Fundamental Defense Capability Reinforcement","Japan will promote efforts to fundamentally reinforce defense capabilities, based on the National Security Strategy and other documents148.",""],[1,"59","1","Defense Equipment and Facility Resilience Improvement","the government will promote improving the number of operationally available equipment, securing ammunition and fuel, and improving resiliency of defense facilities, etc.",""],[1,"59","1","Defense Procurement Efficiency and Rationalization Reform","the government will thoroughly implement efforts to further improve efficiency and rationalize procurement including through utilizing the long-term contract act149, whose effect became permanent.",""],[1,"59","1","Defense Human Resources and Working Conditions Programme","The government will reinforce the human resource base by securing talented personnel, improving living and working environment, and improving treatment",""],[1,"59","1","Defense Medical Function Enhancement","while also continuously enhancing medical functions, such as autonomously securing blood.",""],[1,"59","1","Defense Industry Base Development","Japan will build a powerful and sustainable defense industry",""],[1,"59","1","Defense Equipment and Technology Transfer Promotion","promote the transfer of defense equipment and technology by steadily enforcing the Act on Enhancing Defense Production and Technology bases150.",""],[1,"59","1","Defense Research and Advanced Technology Utilization","The government will also work on research and development and make efforts to use advanced commercial/basic technologies.",""],[1,"59","1","Next-Generation Fighter Aircraft Joint Development","We will promote the joint development of the next-generation fighter aircraft through the Global Combat Air Programme (GCAP) International Government Organization.",""],[1,"59","2","JSDF Joint Operations Command Establishment","the JSDF Joint Operations Command, which is to be newly established",""],[1,"59","2","Japan-U.S. Alliance Deterrence and Response Strengthening","We will reinforce join Japan-U.S. Alliance deterrence and response capabilities of the Japan-U.S. Alliance",""],[1,"59","2","Security Collaboration with Like-Minded Countries","while also reinforcing collaboration with like-minded countries and others",""],[1,"59","2","U.S. Forces Realignment and Base-Related Measures","The government will promote the realignment of U.S. Forces in Japan and the base-related measures.",""],[1,"59","3","Defense Capability Reinforcement Financing Mechanism","With regard to financial resources for the fundamental reinforcement of defense capabilities, the government will secure these financial resources in line with the Defense Buildup Program, etc. including through agile and flexible approaches.",""],[1,"60","2","Defense Research and Development Advancement","Japan will advance efforts in the areas that complement and are inseparable from the fundamental reinforcement of the defense capabilities, namely research and development",""],[1,"60","2","Defense-Related Public Infrastructure Development","Japan will advance efforts in the areas that complement and are inseparable from the fundamental reinforcement of the defense capabilities, namely, public infrastructure development",""],[1,"60","2","International Deterrence Cooperation Initiative","Japan will advance efforts in the areas that complement and are inseparable from the fundamental reinforcement of the defense capabilities, namely, international cooperation to enhance deterrence capabilities of Japan and like-minded countries",""],[1,"60","2","Inter-Ministerial Defense Coordination Structure","while also developing a proper structure of relevant ministries and agencies",""]],"34":[[1,"61","3","Rule-Based International Order Strengthening","Japan will maintain and strengthen a free and open international order based on the rule of law",""],[1,"61","3","International Economic Security Cooperation","ensure economic security in cooperation and collaboration with its ally and like-minded countries, etc.",""],[1,"61","4","Whole-of-Government Economic Security Promotion System","We will strengthen the whole-of-government system for promoting economic security with the National Security Secretariat serving as a control tower.",""],[1,"61","4","Economic Security Intelligence Capability Development","In order to strengthen intelligence capabilities that will contribute to economic security, necessary systems for collecting and analyzing information, including human intelligence, will be developed.",""],[1,"61","4","Local Government Economic Security Coordination","We will collaborate with local governments on economic security.",""],[1,"61","5","Economic Security and Resilient Supply Chain Measures","The government will steadily implement the Economic Security Promotion Act159 and strengthen efforts while also inspecting risks inherent in industry.",""],[1,"61","6","Information Collection and Analysis Function Improvement","This includes the improvement of information collection and analysis functions of the Information-technology Promotion Agency, Japan (IPA) and the National Institute of Information and Communications Technology.",""],[1,"62","1","Advanced Key Technologies Development","developing advanced key technologies",""],[1,"62","1","Technology Leakage Prevention Measures","the government will advance measures against technology leakage with the aim of promoting international cooperation",""],[1,"62","1","Safety and Security Think Tank Establishment","proceed with preparatory work for the establishment of a think tank related to safety and security",""],[1,"62","1","Basic Infrastructure System Review","We will continuously review the basic infrastructure system, including the addition of the medical field",""],[1,"62","1","Critical Infrastructure Resilience Development","In critical infrastructure areas, we will build up infrastructure resilience to address vulnerabilities, including improving autonomy in international communications",""],[1,"62","2","Critical Economic Security Information Protection Act Implementation Preparation","The government will proceed with the preparation for the implementation of the Act on the Protection and Utilization of Critical Economic Security Information160.",""],[1,"62","3","Technology Leakage Prevention and Investment Screening","The government will take measures preventing technology leakage by working on strengthening the relevant system and ensuring the effectiveness of investment screening under the Foreign Exchange and Foreign Trade Act161",""],[1,"62","3","Export Control System Review","to control the export and technologies, including the review of the system",""],[1,"62","3","Research Security and Integrity Measures","to ensure research security and integrity",""],[1,"62","3","International Student and Researcher Screening","to strengthen the screening for the acceptance of international students and researchers",""],[1,"62","3","Economic Coercion Response Measures","Under the policy of not accepting economic coercion, we will proceed with necessary measures.",""],[1,"62","3","Implementation of Relevant Sanctions","In light of Russia's aggression against Ukraine, Japan will work to effectively implement relevant sanctions.",""],[1,"62","3","Data and Information Protection Measures","We will consider necessary measures for data and information protection.",""],[1,"62","4","Important Facility and Remote Island Land Use Regulation","the government will proceed with measures under the Act on the Review and Regulation of the Use of Real Estate Surrounding Important Facilities and on Remote Territorial Islands",""],[1,"62","4","Nationwide Review of Foreign Land Use","further reviews, including responses to the management and use of land nationwide by foreigners",""]],"35":[[1,"62","6","Disaster Risk Reduction Budget Mobilization","we will secure necessary and sufficient budgets",""],[1,"62","6","Integrated Hard and Soft Disaster Risk Reduction","appropriately combine self-help, mutual assistance, and public assistance, and strongly promote efforts that integrate hard and soft measures",""],[1,"63","1","Five-Year Disaster Prevention and National Resilience Acceleration Plan Implementation","The government will continue to steadily promote the engagement based on the Five-Year Acceleration Plan for Disaster Prevention, Disaster Mitigation, and Building National Resilience",""],[1,"63","1","Mid-term National Resilience Plan Formulation","we will accelerate discussions to formulate the Mid-term Plan for the Implementation of National Resilience to the maximum extent possible, including the evaluation of the implementation status of the relevant measures, and will start to formulate the Mid-term Plan for the Implementation of National Resilience in early FY 2024",""],[1,"63","2","Watershed Flood Control Development and Management","the government will accelerate and deepen watershed flood control in light of the effects of future climate change",""],[1,"63","2","Aging Infrastructure and Earthquake Resistance Measures","accelerate measures for aging infrastructure and earthquake resistance",""],[1,"63","2","National Disaster Support Systems and TEC-FORCE","expand and strengthen national disaster support systems and functions such as TEC-FORCE",""],[1,"63","2","Embankment Safety Measures","further strengthen embankment safety measures",""],[1,"63","2","Forest Improvement Measures","forest improvement",""],[1,"63","2","Mountain Settlement Measures","mountain settlement measures",""],[1,"63","2","Disaster Prevention Functions at Schools and Evacuation Centers","disaster prevention functions at places such as schools and evacuation centers",""],[1,"63","3","Disaster-Resistant Lifeline Infrastructure Development","In order to strengthen lifelines such as transportation, communication, and energy, which form the basis of economic development, the government will promote disaster-resistant transportation networks such as eliminating missing links, establishing disaster prevention bases at ports, the elimination of electricity poles, and measures against heavy snow, etc.",""],[1,"63","4","Advanced Disaster Risk Information and Prediction System","the sophistication of disaster risk reduction information such as more accurate predictions of stationary linear mesoscale convective systems and floods using the next geostationary meteorological satellites",""],[1,"63","4","Firefighting and Disaster Management Digital Transformation","the development and introduction of firefighting and DX for disaster management",""],[1,"63","4","Disaster Prevention Science and Technology Development","disaster prevention science and technology",""],[1,"64","1","Land-Use Integrated Disaster Mitigation","take measures to mitigate disasters that are integrated with land use",""],[1,"64","1","Household Earthquake Insurance Enrollment","promote enrollment in earthquake insurance for households",""],[1,"64","2","Timeline Disaster Preparedness Implementation","implement Timeline Disaster Preparedness by promoting the use of Weather Disaster Risk Reduction Advisor and regional disaster prevention managers",""],[1,"64","3","Volcanic Disaster Countermeasures","the government will promote measures against volcanic disasters",""],[1,"64","3","Volcano Research Promotion","the research at the Headquarters for Volcano Research Promotion",""],[1,"64","3","Specialized Human Resources Training and Retention","the training and continuation guaranteed of specialized human resources",""]],"36":[[1,"66","3","Earthquake-Resilient Water and Sewerage Infrastructure","make water supply, sewerage and other infrastructure earthquake-resistant",""],[1,"66","3","Alternative Water Source Security","secure alternative water sources such as groundwater178",""],[1,"66","3","Liquefaction Risk Mitigation Measures","take measures against liquefaction",""],[1,"66","3","Peninsula Transport Network Strengthening","strengthen networks such as roads, railways, ports and airports in the peninsula",""],[1,"66","3","Roadside Station Base Function Strengthening","strengthen the base functions of roadside stations",""],[1,"66","3","Communications and Broadcasting Network Strengthening","strengthen communications and broadcasting networks",""],[1,"66","3","Disaster-Affected Area Recovery and Reconstruction","help afflicted areas recover and rebuild from disasters",""],[1,"65","4","Affected People Livelihoods and Infrastructure Reconstruction","We will continue to make full efforts to rebuild the lives and livelihoods of affected people as soon as possible, prevent disaster-related deaths, restore infrastructure and other facilities",""],[1,"65","4","Publicly Funded Demolition and Authority Extinguishment Registration","promote the dismantling financed by public funds and the authority extinguishment registration",""],[1,"65","4","Regional Reconstruction Town Development Planning","support the formulation of reconstruction town development plans based on regional characteristics",""],[1,"65","4","Agriculture Forestry Fisheries and Culture Reconstruction","creatively reconstruct agriculture, forestry, fisheries, and culture and arts",""],[1,"65","4","Ishikawa Prefecture Reconstruction Fund Support","The national government will also support the efforts financed by the reconstruction fund of Ishikawa Prefecture and the like",""],[1,"65","4","Okunoto Digital Lifeline Development","Through support for the development of Okunoto Digital lifeline and the use of new technologies, the project aims to make reconstruction of Okunoto a model for regional revitalization in areas with declining population",""],[1,"65","4","Noto Region Tourism Demand Stimulation","We will work to revive tourism by taking careful measures to stimulate demand for travel in the Noto region in accordance with the reconstruction situation",""]],"37":[[1,"64","4","Tohoku Earthquake and Tsunami Recovery Project","The government aims to fulfill the role of the recovery project for the second-term recovery and revitalization period in the earthquake and tsunami affected areas.",""],[1,"64","4","Mental Care Support for Disaster-Affected Areas","To this end, we will properly address the relevant issues such as mental care, by, for example, utilizing government-wide policies and measures.",""],[1,"64","4","Nuclear Disaster Area Reconstruction and Revitalization","The national government will continue to play a leading role in the reconstruction and revitalization of areas hit by the nuclear power disaster, which require medium-to long-term measures.",""],[1,"64","4","Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant Decommissioning","We will safely and steadily proceed with our efforts concerning the decommissioning of Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant.",""],[1,"65","1","Safety and Livelihood Continuity Measures","measures to ensure safety, prevent adverse impacts on reputation, and support continuation of livelihoods.",""],[1,"65","1","Removal of Import Restrictions on Japanese Food Products","Japan will strongly request the immediate repeal of import restrictions on Japanese food products by certain countries and regions.",""],[1,"65","1","Managed Recycling Sites for Removed Soil","the government will proceed with approach to develop a system for the creation of sites for the managed recycling of removed soil.",""],[1,"65","1","Living Conditions Improvement in Evacuated Areas","the government will promote improvement of living conditions such as medical care and education",""],[1,"65","1","Relocation and Settlement Promotion","promote relocation and settlement.",""],[1,"65","1","Evacuation Order Lifting and Area Reconstruction","we will firstly proceed with the effort to lift the evacuation order for the Specified Living Areas for Returnees.",""],[1,"65","1","Fukushima Innovation Coast Framework","We will develop the Fukushima Innovation Coast Framework",""],[1,"65","1","Fukushima Institute for Research, Education and Innovation","promote initiatives such as the Fukushima Institute for Research, Education and Innovation",""],[1,"65","1","Fukushima Plan for a New Energy Society","promote initiatives such as ... the Fukushima Plan for a New Energy Society.",""],[1,"65","1","Livelihood Recovery and New Industry Development","We will promote reconstruction through the livelihood recovery, the creation of new industries",""],[1,"65","1","Forest and Forestry Regeneration","the regeneration of forests and forestry",""],[1,"65","1","Culture and Arts-Based Community Revitalization","local community revitalization through culture and arts",""],[1,"65","1","Exchange Population Expansion","the expansion of exchange population.",""],[1,"65","1","Post-Period Reconstruction Planning","We will consider how the reconstruction after the current period should be.",""]],"38":[[1,"60","1","Expenditure Reform Continuation","the government will continue to work on the continuation of expenditure reform",""],[1,"60","1","Settlement Surplus Account Utilization","the utilization of settlement surplus accounts",""],[1,"60","1","Non-Tax Revenue Mobilization","the securing of non-tax revenues",""],[1,"60","1","Fiscal Tax Reform and Legislative Measures","The tax measures shall be deliberated in accordance with the basic directions specified in the Outline of the Tax Reform for Fiscal 2023151 and the Outline of the Tax Reform for Fiscal 2024152, and necessary legislative measures shall be taken at an appropriate time based on the results of the deliberations.",""],[1,"67","4","Expenditure Efficiency Budgeting Mechanism","continued to formulate a budget in line with benchmarks for expenditures and worked to increase the expenditure efficiency",""],[1,"67","5","Government Expenditure Reform","expenditure reform efforts will continue under the Economic Growth Achieved Case indicated in Economic and Fiscal Projections for Medium to Long Term Analysis179.",""],[1,"68","2","Economic and Fiscal Policy Resource Allocation Reform","change the quality of economic and fiscal policies from crisis response to resource allocation focusing on raising the potential growth rate, while responding to price hikes such as higher cost of living, wages, and interest rates",""],[1,"68","2","Sustainable Fiscal Structure and Public Debt Reduction","secure a sustainable fiscal structure that achieves a stable reduction of public debt-to-GDP ratio in normal times",""],[1,"68","4","Integrated Economic and Fiscal Reform Programme","The government will continue to promote integrated economic and fiscal reforms.",""],[1,"69","1","Public Service Delivery Efficiency Reform","making the public sector more efficient through the expansion or collective delivery of public services or the commercialization of public service",""],[1,"69","1","Incentive Reform and Policy Visualization","carrying out incentive reforms and visualization",""],[1,"69","1","Advanced Practice Horizontal Deployment","promoting behavior change through horizontal deployment of advanced cases",""],[1,"69","1","Multi-Year Fiscal Resource Integration","we will also consider financial resources in an integrated manner and balance expenditures and revenues over multiple fiscal years",""],[1,"69","1","Single-Year Budget Principle Reform","The government will work to correct the negative effects of the single-fiscal year budget principle.",""],[1,"69","1","Evidence-Based Policy Making and Wise Spending","the government will further strengthen EBPM and thoroughly implement wise spending",""],[1,"69","2","Fiscal Consolidation and Public Debt Reduction Initiative","The government will resolutely pursue fiscal consolidation and work on achieving the current target.",""],[1,"70","1","Situational Economic Monitoring and Verification Mechanism","The government will therefore undertake the necessary verification depending on the situation.",""],[1,"70","2","Current Expenditure Reform","the government will continue current expenditure reform efforts181 during the three years from FY 2025 to FY 2027",""],[1,"70","2","Flexible Macroeconomic Management","The government will work to raise the potential growth rate while working on flexible macroeconomic management.",""],[1,"70","8","Public Expenditure Reform","The government will continue constant efforts for the expenditure reform during the three years from FY 2022 to FY 2024",""],[1,"71","1","Evidence-Based Economic and Fiscal Reform Process","measures to strengthen EBPM and the reform process of integrated economic and fiscal reforms by the end of this year",""],[1,"71","1","Economic and Fiscal Reform Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","monitor, examine, and evaluate the progress of the reform every year",""]],"39":[[1,"67","4","Child and Child-Rearing Policy Expansion","expanding child and child-rearing policies",""],[1,"67","4","COVID-19 and Cost-of-Living Policy Response","made flexible policy responses to COVID-19 and the high cost of living",""],[1,"71","3","Resilient Sustainable Social Security System","We also need to establish a resilient and sustainable social security system that can withstand medium- to long-term structural changes in society based on the long-term estimates.",""],[1,"71","3","Task Shifting and Task Sharing Reform","promotion of task shifting/sharing",""],[1,"71","3","All-Generational Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","all-generational reskilling and upskilling",""],[1,"71","3","Lifelong Active Society Promotion","realization of a lifelong active society in which everyone, including women and the elderly, can play an active role according to their motivation",""],[1,"71","3","Future Strategy for Children Implementation","response to the declining birthrate through effective implementation of Future Strategy for Children",""],[1,"71","4","Medical and Long-Term Care Spending Reform","thoroughly implement wise spending through constant reforms in medical and long-term care, and to curb the rise in the insurance premium burden",""],[1,"71","4","Integrated Economic and Fiscal Reform","we will steadily promote the integrated economic and fiscal reforms in accordance with the \"time horizon\" defined by the Reform",""],[1,"72","1","Social Security Vision Public Information Initiative","the government will provide the public with easy-to-understand information about the future vision of social security for all generations",""]],"40":[[1,"71","3","Medical and Long-Term Care Technology and Data Utilization","productivity improvement through thorough utilization of advanced technologies and data such as medical and long-term care DX, ICT, and robots",""],[1,"72","1","Medical and Long-Term Care Delivery System Improvement","Improving medical and long-term care delivery systems",""],[1,"72","2","High-Quality Medical and Long-Term Care Service System","it is necessary to ensure a system for providing high-quality and efficient medical and long-term care services while making effective use of limited resources.",""],[1,"72","2","Government-Wide Medical and Long-Term Care DX Promotion","strong promotion of medical and long-term care DX by the entire government",""],[1,"72","2","Robotics, Digital Technology, and ICT Utilization","utilization of robot and digital technologies, ICT, and online medical examinations",""],[1,"72","2","Online Medical Examination Service Expansion","online medical examinations",""],[1,"72","2","Medical and Long-Term Care Task Shifting","task shifting/sharing",""],[1,"72","2","Medical Care Functional Differentiation","functional differentiation",""],[1,"72","2","Medical Care Coordination Mechanism","coordination of medical care",""],[1,"72","3","Primary Care Doctor Functions Development System","The government will develop a system in which the functions of primary care doctors are demonstrated from the viewpoint of the public",""],[1,"72","3","Regional Medical and Social Welfare Cooperation Mechanism","utilize regional medical cooperation promotion corporations and social welfare cooperation promotion corporations",""],[1,"72","3","Emergency Medical Care Systems","secure emergency medical care systems",""],[1,"72","3","Sustainable Doctor Helicopter Operations","promote sustainable doctor helicopter operations",""],[1,"72","3","Universal Perinatal Care Provision","secure perinatal care in which a pregnant woman can safely give birth regardless of where she lives",""],[1,"72","3","Prefectural Health Governance Strengthening","strengthen prefectural governance",""],[1,"72","3","Community Health Care Visions Outreach Support","the national government will back up the relevant outreach efforts toward 2025",""],[1,"72","3","Expanded Community Health Care Visions Coverage","we will expand the coverage of the Community Health Care Visions to include the entire regional medical care provision system",""],[1,"72","3","Integrated Medical Care System Role and Financing Reform","we will clarify the functions of medical institutions, examine the responsibilities and authorities of prefectures, the roles of municipalities, as well as the ideal form of financial support, including legislative measures, and reach a conclusion by the end of 2024",""],[1,"73","2","Medical Institution Cooperation for Long-Term Care","strengthen cooperation with medical institutions",""],[1,"73","2","Technology and Provider Upscaling for Long-Term Care","promote the use of technology, collaboration and upscaling of long-term care service providers",""],[1,"73","2","Long-Term Care Provider Management Transparency","promote the visualization of management conditions of long-term care service providers and medical institutions, including financial information such as assets and salaries by job type etc.",""],[1,"73","2","Long-Term Care Workforce Conditions Improvement","we will work to improve wages, reduce the workload, and encourage the relevant organizations/providers to improve the working environment",""],[1,"73","2","Long-Term Care Human Resources Recruitment","the government will proceed with measures to secure human resources, including foreign long-term care personnel",""],[1,"73","2","Long-Term Care Service Provision System Planning","examine the ideal vision to secure a medium- to long-term care service provision system, taking into account the regional axis and the time axis",""]],"41":[[1,"81","1","Five-Year Preconception Care Strategy","The government will formulate a five-year strategy for preconception care",""],[1,"81","1","Preconception Care Consultation and Support System","including the establishment of a care system that offers consultation and support for those in need",""],[1,"81","1","Postpartum Care Services","postpartum care services",""],[1,"81","1","Newborn Mass Screening Programme","newborn mass screening",""],[1,"81","1","Newborn Hearing Testing Programme","newborn hearing tests",""],[1,"81","1","Infant Medical Examination Services","medical examinations for infants",""],[1,"81","1","Infertility and Pregnancy Loss Consultation Support","provide consultation support for those who suffer infertility or those who have experienced miscarriage, stillbirth, or recurrent pregnancy loss",""],[1,"81","2","Support Programme for Young Expecting Mothers","supporting young expecting mothers",""],[1,"81","1","Public-Private Life Design Support","the public and private sectors will cooperate to promote life design support",""]],"43":[[1,"79","1","Local Birthrate and Childcare Support Models","verify the respective implementation models for effective measures to address the declining birthrate and for child and child care support through public-private partnerships in accordance with local circumstances",""],[1,"80","3","Child and Child Care Support Act Implementation","The government will steadily implement the amended Child and Child Care Support Act209 and the other measures included in the Acceleration Plan210",""],[1,"80","3","Expanded Child Allowance Programme","the drastic expansion of child allowance from October this year",""],[1,"80","3","Childbirth Cost Reduction Support","reduction of economic burden on matters such as childbirth",""],[1,"80","3","Housing Support for Families with Children","strengthening of housing support",""],[1,"80","3","Family Accompanying Consultation Support","accompanying consultation support",""],[1,"80","3","Nursery and Kindergarten Teacher Treatment Improvement","improvement of treatment for nursery teachers and kindergarten teachers",""],[1,"80","3","Nursery Teacher Placement Standards Improvement","improvement of placement standards for nursery teachers",""],[1,"80","3","Universal Nursery School Access System","a system where anyone can attend a nursery school",""],[1,"80","3","After-School Child Support Measures","measures for after-school children",""],[1,"80","3","Coparenting Leave Support Benefits","the establishment of coparenting-leave support benefits",""],[1,"80","3","Reduced Working Hours Benefits for Childcare","benefits for reduced working hours for childcare",""],[1,"80","3","Child and Child-Rearing Expenditure Reform","the government will promote thorough expenditure reform based on the Reform Process",""],[1,"80","3","Child and Child-Rearing Support Contribution System","introduce the System of Child and Child-rearing Support Contribution from fiscal 2026",""],[1,"80","3","Society-Wide Awareness Initiative for Child Support","the government and the private sector as the “two wheels of a vehicle” will work together to promote initiatives to foster awareness of supporting children and families with children in society as a whole",""],[1,"80","5","Child and Child Care Support Act Revision","Act for Partial Revision of the Child and Child Care Support Act (Act No. 47 of 2024).",""],[1,"80","5","Accelerated Child and Child Care Support Plan","Plan to accelerate child and child care support based on the Future Strategy for Children (Cabinet Decision on December 22, 2023).",""],[1,"81","1","Multifunctional Childcare Services in Declining-Population Areas","including the maintenance of childcare functions through multifunctional facilities in areas with a declining population",""],[1,"92","1","Declining Birthrate and Child Policy Strengthening Measures","measures include those to combat the declining birthrate and drastically strengthen child policies",""]],"46":[[1,"80","4","Child and Youth Participation Promotion","promoting the expression of opinions and views and participation of children and young people as independent actors holding rights",""],[1,"80","4","Supportive Environment for Youth-Led Organizations","we will work toward the development of an environment in which continuous activities of organizations mainly led by young people will be promoted",""],[1,"80","4","Early Childhood Growth Quality Improvement","we will improve the quality of growth up to early childhood based on “the First 100 Months of Growth Vision”",""],[1,"80","4","Local Government and Private Organization Support for Ibasho","provide support to local governments and private organizations based on the Guidelines for the Creation of Ibasho (place where one",""],[1,"81","1","Prevention of Sexual Violence against Children","The government will promote comprehensive measures to prevent sexual violence against children",""],[1,"81","1","Prevention of Sexual Violence against Children Act","including Prevention of Sexual Violence against Children Act",""],[1,"81","1","Life Safety Education for Children","the Life Safety Education",""],[1,"81","1","Rehabilitation of Sexual Violence Offenders","rehabilitation of offenders",""],[1,"81","1","Treatment for Sexual Preference Disorders","treatment for sexual preference disorders",""],[1,"81","1","Child Safety Measures","We will also promote child safety measures",""],[1,"82","1","Child Suicide Prevention Measures","The government will strengthen measures against suicide among children",""],[1,"82","1","Child Death Review Prevention Mechanism","will promote the CDR (Child Death Review) for the prevention of child death.",""],[1,"82","1","School Bullying Prevention Measures","Measures to prevent bullying ... will be strengthened.",""],[1,"82","1","Youth Sound Development Programme","Efforts will be made to promote the sound development of youths based on the Basic Plan for the Promotion of Education.",""]],"47":[[1,"82","1","High-Quality Public Education Revitalization","We will strongly promote the revitalization of high-quality public education.",""],[1,"82","2","Flexible Education Curricula Development","the government will promote efforts toward the realization of flexible education curricula",""],[1,"82","2","GIGA School Program Expansion and Evaluation","steadily promoting the GIGA School Program after conducting a thorough verification of its effects based on data",""],[1,"82","2","Public Education Quality Enhancement","we will work to revitalize high-quality public education suitable for the contemporary Reiwa, including the improvement of the quality of high school education beyond the compulsory education stage and aim to further enhance school education in Japan",""],[1,"84","1","Schools and Support Centers for Chronic Absenteeism","promoting the establishment of special schools for chronical absentees and educational support centers inside and outside schools and strengthening their functions",""],[1,"84","1","Inclusive Special Needs Education Management Model","developing systems and environments for the enhancement of Special Needs Education including construction of an inclusive school management model",""],[1,"84","1","Nationwide Junior High Evening Classes","promoting the establishment and strengthening of evening classes at junior high schools nationwide",""],[1,"84","1","Early Childhood Education and Childcare Quality Improvement","the government will promote the qualitative improvement of education and childcare for children in early childhood and the transition period to the elementary school education stage",""],[1,"84","1","Experiential and Reading Activities for Child Development","experiential activities such as experiencing nature, and reading activities to foster rich sensitivity and creativity",""],[1,"84","1","Career and Vocational Education Promotion","career education and vocational education, etc.",""],[1,"84","1","School Attendance Support System Reform","the government will steadily implement system revisions such as the new system for school attendance support and will enhance the management structure",""],[1,"85","1","High School Education Expense Reduction and Quality Improvement Initiative","At the high school level also, the government will promote the reduction of educational expenses while improving the quality of education.",""]],"48":[[1,"82","3","Teacher Work-Style Reform","The government will further accelerate work-style reforms",""],[1,"82","3","Teacher Treatment Improvement Policy","improve treatment",""],[1,"82","3","Teacher Instruction System Enhancement","expand and enhance the instruction systems",""],[1,"82","3","Highly Qualified Teacher Training Support","provide training support",""],[1,"83","1","School Work-Style Reform and Efficiency Improvement","In addition to promoting the optimization of duties undertaken by schools and teachers and the improvement of work efficiency through DX, the PDCA cycle will be strengthened by visualizing the state of work-style reform efforts in schools, and teachers’ hours spent after working time will be thoroughly reduced.",""],[1,"83","1","Teacher Salary and Allowance System Reform","While taking into account the recommendation, the government will consider the salary system toward a well-defined one according to job details and responsibilities, such as the creation of new positions and grades, the addition of allowances according to the importance and burden of the duties of the homeroom teacher, and the improvement of various allowances such as administrator ones.",""],[1,"83","1","Expansion of Teacher Assignments and Support Staff","We will work to expand the subject-based teacher assignments in elementary schools; increase the number of teaching staff, such as assigning more teachers in charge of guidance and counseling to junior high schools; and enhance allocation of assistant staff such as Vice principals and assistant principals’ management support staff.",""],[1,"83","1","Improved School Class Sizes and Instruction Systems","Moreover, we will create desirable educational environments and instruction systems for junior high and other schools, utilizing the verified multifaceted effects achieved in 35-student elementary school classes.",""],[1,"83","1","Local Teacher Recruitment and Professional Development","The government will work to utilize Admission Quota for applicants wishing to work as local teachers, teacher training to enhance development, enhance training, including strengthening management skills of administrator",""],[1,"83","1","Graduate Teacher Scholarship Repayment Support","implement support for the return of scholarships at the graduate school level, and further study this matter to include such return at the undergraduate level.",""],[1,"83","2","Community Schools and Community Cooperation Initiative","the government will accelerate integrated initiatives for community schools and community cooperation activities for learning and education",""],[1,"83","2","School Club Activities Transition Initiative","initiatives for the transition of club activities",""],[1,"84","2","School Club Activity Instructor Recruitment","Includes securing club activity instructors and other relevant leaders",""],[1,"84","2","School Club Activity Governance Coordination System","developing systems for governing bodies and implementing entities, including the assignment of coordinators",""],[1,"84","2","School Club Participation Cost Support","working on environmental arrangements in light of issues such as support for shouldering participation costs",""]],"49":[[1,"84","1","Higher Education Function Review","the government will reach a certain conclusion by the end of fiscal 2024 on the quality, access, and size of higher education in order to strengthen the functions of such education",""],[1,"84","1","Deferred Tuition Payment System","promptly reaching a conclusion about the full-scale introduction of a deferred payment system for tuition fees",""],[1,"85","1","Research Quality Enhancement Mechanism","Construction of a mechanism to enhance the quality of research",""],[1,"85","2","University Education, Research, and Governance Reform","the government will promote integrated reforms of education, research, and governance at universities",""],[1,"85","2","Evidence-Based Policy Making for Science and Technology","strengthening EBPM in the overall science and technology policies",""],[1,"85","2","University and Private School Core Funding Support","the government will secure sufficient basic expenses such as operating grants and subsidies for private schools",""],[1,"85","2","Scientific Research Funding Reform","we will constantly review and enhance research funding, including the reform of the Grants-in-Aid for Scientific Research system",""],[1,"85","2","Large-Scale Research Facility Development Partnership","we will promote the strategic development, utilization, and upgrade of large-scale research facilities through public-private partnerships, etc.",""],[1,"85","2","Research Digital Transformation Initiative","improve productivity through research DX",""],[1,"85","2","Young Researcher Compensation Improvement","improve the compensation of young researchers",""],[1,"85","2","Women’s Participation in Research and R&D Management","promote the active participation of female researchers and R&D management personnel",""],[1,"85","2","University Industry-Academia-Government Co-Creation Centers","turn campuses into co-creation centers through industry-academia-government collaboration",""],[1,"85","2","University Hospital Physician Work-Style Reform","promote work-style reforms for physicians in university hospitals while ensuring the quality of education, research, and medical care functions in these hospitals",""],[1,"85","3","Science Council Independent Legal Personality Reform","we will proceed with deliberations on the necessary legislation for the Science Council to become an organization with an independent legal personality so as to ensure its thorough independence, autonomous evolution, as well as transparency and governance.",""]],"50":[[1,"85","5","PPP/PFI and New Technology Utilization","the utilization of PPP/PFI and new technologies, in order to build sustainable local communities",""],[1,"85","5","Efficient Town Development and Infrastructure Management","we will work on the greater efficiency and sophistication in town development and infrastructure maintenance/management",""],[1,"86","2","Compact Urban Development and Infrastructure Renewal Planning","While promoting making wide-area urban areas more compact, the government will consider the priorities and other matters concerning measures to address the aging infrastructure (repair, renewal, aggregation, consolidation, etc.) based on town development plans such as location optimization plans, before the implementation.",""],[1,"86","2","Architectural and Urban Digital Transformation","We will promote Architectural and Urban Digital Transformation, such as Base Registry, including real estate IDs and 3D models (architectural BIM227, PLATEAU), and promote the creation of new services through the sophistication of town development and public-private data collaboration.",""],[1,"87","3","Small Concessions Using Vacant Housing","We will promote the spread of small concessions, etc., that utilize existing stock of vacant houses, etc.",""],[1,"87","5","Smooth Land-Use Conversion Measures","the government will introduce measures for smooth conversion of land use, including the conversion into non-residential land use.",""],[1,"87","5","Vacant House Prevention and Management Measures","the government will promote comprehensive actions by controlling the occurrence of vacant houses through the back-up of local governments, and properly managing and disposing such houses.",""],[1,"87","5","Vacant House Utilization and Distribution Mechanism","we will expand the use of such houses by expanding the relevant distribution mechanism and promoting dual-area residence.",""],[1,"87","5","Unclaimed Land Registration and Consultation Measures","We will also promote measures for unclaimed land in an integrated and comprehensive manner, including the dissemination of the mandatory application for inheritance registration, the strengthening of consultation systems",""],[1,"87","5","Cadastral Survey and Land Mapping Initiative","conducting cadastral surveys and preparing maps",""],[1,"88","1","Public Land Appraiser Recruitment Mechanism","Efforts will be made to secure real estate appraisers who support public land appraisals.",""],[1,"88","1","Condominium Management and Regeneration Facilitation","we will work to facilitate proper management of condominiums234 and their regeneration.",""],[1,"88","5","Fixed-Rate Housing Loan Refinancing Facilitation","efforts will be made to facilitate refinancing of housing loans to fixed-rate loans.",""]],"51":[[1,"85","5","Sustainable Land and Water Resource Management","we will work on ... the sustainable use and management of land and water resources",""],[1,"88","2","Comprehensive Watershed Water Management","We will also promote the watershed comprehensive water management",""],[1,"88","2","Hydroelectric Power Generation Reinforcement","the reinforcing of hydroelectric power generation on a watershed-by-watershed basis",""],[1,"88","2","Water Supply and Sewerage Facility Reorganization","the reorganization of water supply/sewerage facilities",""],[1,"88","5","Local-Condition-Based Wastewater Treatment Facility Use","we will promote the use of wastewater treatment facilities, including Johkasou, based on local conditions.",""]],"52":[[1,"86","3","Strategic Preventive Infrastructure Maintenance Programme","promote full-scale conversion into preventive maintenance and the sophistication/efficiency of maintenance/management as well as the optimization of public stock by implementing wide-area and strategic infrastructure management",""],[1,"86","3","Public-Private Infrastructure Management Collaboration Mechanism","promoting collaboration between business operators or between private and public sectors",""],[1,"86","3","State-Owned Property Utilization Programme","We will also utilize the existing state-owned property effectively.",""],[1,"86","3","Infrastructure Maintenance Financing Measures","the government will consider financial resource measures, etc.",""],[1,"86","5","i-Construction2.0 Automation and Productivity Programme","The government will promote i-Construction2.0, which aims at automation and labor saving, in order to achieve at least 30% labor saving and 1.5 times productivity improvement at construction sites by 2040.",""],[1,"86","5","Cross-Sectoral Infrastructure Data Development and Disclosure","We will promote cross-sectoral development and disclosure of infrastructure data 228",""],[1,"86","5","Online Administrative Procedures","online administrative procedures",""],[1,"86","5","Infrastructure Digital Transformation Acceleration","will accelerate infrastructure DX",""],[1,"86","6","High-Stock-Effect Project Prioritization","we will focus on the projects with high stock effects in view of demographic trends",""],[1,"86","6","Cost-Benefit Analysis Transparency Reform","while improving the objectivity and transparency of cost-benefit analysis",""],[1,"86","7","Public Works Efficiency Improvement","We will work on making public works projects more efficient",""],[1,"86","8","Construction Data Platforms and Utilization Initiatives","Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism Data Platform, and Project LINKS, which will engage in EBPM and business creation through data preparation and utilization.",""],[1,"87","1","Medium- to Long-Term Investment Planning","investment from a medium- to long-term outlook so that private businesses can make capital investments and develop human resources with peace of mind.",""]],"53":[[1,"88","4","Local Government Digital Transformation","promote local government DX through the thorough implementation of digital technologies such as AI and RPA",""],[1,"88","4","Local Government General Revenue Stabilization Mechanism","The government will ensure that the total amount of general revenue sources necessary for stable fiscal management of local governments, including those receiving local allocation tax grants, shall be maintained substantially at the same level as that of the FY 2024 Fiscal Plan of Local Governments, and not below.",""],[1,"89","3","Local Government Digital Transformation for Administrative and Fiscal Efficiency","Improving administrative and fiscal efficiency through local government DX",""],[1,"89","4","Online Application and One-Stop Counter Reform","we will work on front-yard reforms, such as online application and \"one-stop counter without writing,\"",""],[1,"89","4","Local Government Core Systems Standardization","backyard reforms, such as unification and standardization of core service systems",""],[1,"89","4","eLTAX Public Money Payment Expansion","utilization of eLTAX for payment of public money other than local taxes",""],[1,"89","4","Prefectural-Municipal Cooperation and Human Resources Pool","Prefectural governments and municipalities will establish a system for promoting their cooperation, in which the human resources pool function is to be ensured.",""],[1,"89","4","Local Government Cybersecurity Policy Development","we will promote the formulation of policies for ensuring cyber security in local governments",""],[1,"89","4","Central and Local Government Consultation Chatbot Improvement","progressively improving \"Central/Local Government Consultation Chatbot (Govbot)” from the user perspective",""],[1,"89","5","Stable Local Tax System Development","With the overconcentration of functions in Tokyo persisting, we will endeavor to build a stable local taxes system with less uneven tax source distribution, in light of the uneven distribution status of tax revenues among local governments and the adjustment status of the gaps among their financial capability, in order to prevent an excessive gap in administration services among local governments from being generated.",""],[1,"89","6","Early Consultation Mechanism for Local Government System Planning","When the ministries and agencies have no choice but to make a plan for the form of a system related to local governments, they shall explain it to the six local governments organizations at an early stage.","Cabinet Office"],[1,"89","6","Local Government Administrative Burden Reduction and Review Mechanism","With regard to the existing plans, the national government will reduce the administrative burdens on local governments and publicize annually the status of the review.",""],[1,"89","7","Local Government Digital Transformation Promotion Plan","Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications formulated the Local Government Digital Transformation (DX) Promotion Plan [Version 3.0] (April 24, 2024), which summarizes the priority issues for local governments.","Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications"]],"54":[[1,"79","5","Evidence-Based Policy Management and PDCA Mechanism","promoting PDCA using the numerical targets and other relevant indicators",""],[1,"90","1","Council Selection Mechanism for Priority Policies","the Council on Economic and Fiscal Policy will select important policies and plans, which will be enforced for multiple fiscal years and will have a significant impact on the economy and public finances",""],[1,"90","1","Evidence-Based Policy Development and Verification","the Cabinet Office, the relevant ministries and agencies will formulate policies for evidence development from the budget request stage, set logic models and KPIs, collect data, and proceed with process management through ex post facto verification","Cabinet Office | relevant ministries and agencies"],[1,"90","1","Policy Analysis and Evaluation Systems Development","the relevant systems will be developed while utilizing the research and study functions of the Cabinet Office, the relevant ministries and agencies","Cabinet Office | relevant ministries and agencies"],[1,"90","1","EBPM Results Integration into Budget Formulation","We will consider measures to reflect the results of EBPM efforts and quantitative policy effects in the budget formulation process in the following fiscal year and beyond",""],[1,"90","2","Government Data Linkage and Analysis Infrastructure","promote the development of infrastructure for data linkage/analysis",""],[1,"90","2","EBPM Human Resources Training and Exchange","the training and exchange of EBPM human resources",""],[1,"90","2","Policy Effects Analysis Knowledge Initiative","the accumulation and utilization of knowledge on methods for ascertaining and analyzing policy effects at research institutions and universities",""],[1,"90","2","Administrative Project Review for Government-Wide EBPM","We will utilize the administrative project review sheet system in the budget formulation process to promote EBPM in all budget projects.",""],[1,"90","3","Well-being Indicator Integration in Public Administration","We will promote the use of well-being indicators in public administration",""],[1,"90","3","Next-Generation Economic Indicator Development","We will examine economic indicators that reflect changes in the next generation’s social life and their values",""],[1,"90","3","Official Statistics Digital Transformation","The government will promote official statistics DX",""],[1,"90","3","Private-Sector Big Data Analysis Development","We will also promote the development of analysis and indicators using big data from private companies",""],[1,"92","1","Evidence-Based Policymaking and PDCA Spending Management","We will promote the EBPM and PDCA efforts and ensure wise spending.",""]],"55":[[1,"91","4","Comprehensive Economic Measures Implementation","the government will swiftly and steadily implement the Comprehensive Economic Measures to Completely Overcome Deflation",""],[1,"91","5","Sustainable Price Stability Monetary Policy Management","At the same time, we expect the Bank of Japan to achieve the price stability target of 2 percent in a sustainable and stable manner, while confirming the virtuous cycle between wages and prices, by conducting appropriate monetary policy management in light of economic activity, prices and financial conditions.","Bank of Japan"]],"57":[[1,"9","2","Women’s Regular Employment Promotion","promoting regular employment for women",""],[1,"10","2","Young Generations Income Improvement Policy","We will also improve the income of younger generations",""],[1,"13","1","Parental Work-Life Balance Support","support work-life balance for parents",""],[1,"13","1","Gender Equality and Pay Gap Measures","empower women, address gender pay gaps, and eliminate gender disparities",""],[1,"15","5","Gender Pay Gap Industry Analysis and Issue Identification","the government will identify and analyze the realities of industries with larger gender pay differences, organize the issues that need to be addressed",""],[1,"15","5","Industry Gender Pay Gap Action Plans","encourage these industries to formulate action plans",""],[1,"15","5","Gender Pay Gap Transparency and Analytical Tools","We will also promote the visibility of differences and the development and utilization of tools for analyzing differences.",""],[1,"15","5","White Paper Gender Pay Gap Analysis and Elimination Measures","In the white paper, we will conduct a deeper analysis of pay gaps between men and women and work on creating an environment to eliminate these gaps.",""],[1,"15","6","Non-Regular Worker Regularization Incentive Policy","The government will implement policies to encourage companies to hire non-regular workers as regular employees if they wish.",""],[1,"15","6","Equal Pay for Equal Work Enforcement","Prefectural Labor Bureaus and Labor Standards Inspection Offices more thoroughly enforce the equal pay for equal work.",""],[1,"15","6","Equal Treatment Guidelines Revision","the government will consider revising the current guidelines.",""],[1,"16","1","Employees’ Insurance Package Utilization Promotion","employees’ insurance in parallel with the promotion of utilization of the package for not being conscious of so-called “annual income barriers”4.",""],[1,"18","3","Elderly Worker Participation Case Study Dissemination","compiling and disseminating case studies of companies fostering the active participation of elderly workers",""],[1,"18","3","Elderly Worker Workplace Safety Improvements","improving workplace environments to prevent work-related accidents among elderly individuals",""],[1,"18","3","Workplace Mental Health Measures","strengthening mental health measures including Stress Check Program",""],[1,"18","4","Telework Promotion Policy","working on policies to promote telework",""],[1,"18","4","Inter-Shift Interval System Introduction","facilitating the introduction of inter-shift interval systems",""],[1,"18","4","Optional Three-Day Weekend Promotion","promoting the spread of optional three-day weekends",""],[1,"18","4","Household Chores Support Services Promotion","encourage the appropriate use of services to reduce household chores burdens",""],[1,"18","5","Freelancer Safety and Health Systems Review","The government will conduct research and deliberation on systems for safety and health measures for freelancers, aiming to reach a conclusion by the end of the FY 2024.",""],[1,"18","5","Freelancer Transaction Practice Investigation","the government will investigate actual transaction practices","Japan Fair Trade Commission | Small and Medium Enterprise Agency | Ministry of Health, Labor and Welfare"],[1,"18","5","Freelancer Transaction Enforcement Framework","establish a framework for its enforcement by the Japan Fair Trade Commission, Small and Medium Enterprise Agency, and Ministry of Health, Labor and Welfare.","Japan Fair Trade Commission | Small and Medium Enterprise Agency | Ministry of Health, Labor and Welfare"]],"58":[[1,"6","2","Macroeconomic Management for Growth and Distribution","the government, in cooperation with the Bank of Japan, has conducted appropriate macroeconomic management",""],[1,"8","2","Macroeconomic Policy Coordination and Flexible Management","the government will continue to closely cooperate with the Bank of Japan and flexibly manage macroeconomic policies in response to economic and price conditions.",""],[1,"8","3","Sustainable Fiscal Structure Measures","steadfastly advancing measures to establish a sustainable fiscal structure",""],[1,"8","3","Appropriate Monetary Policy Management","by conducting appropriate monetary policy management in light of economic activity, prices and financial conditions",""],[1,"8","5","Economic and Fiscal Conditions Review Mechanism","The Council on Economic and Fiscal Policy will continue to conduct regular reviews of economic and fiscal conditions, including trends in wages, income, and prices, the status of macroeconomic policy management, including monetary policy, and progress in economic structural reforms.",""],[1,"10","2","All-Generations Social Security System","we will build a social security system for all generations",""],[1,"10","3","Integrated Economy, Public Finance, and Social Security Reform","In this context, we will advance integrated reforms in the economy, public finances, and social security systems, ensuring their coordinated advancement to secure the sustainability of the economy and society.",""],[1,"11","2","Long-Term Economic Growth Reform Programme","We must advance reforms in line with the direction stated above to achieve sustainable economic growth exceeding 1% in real terms even beyond the 2030s, when population decline worsens",""],[1,"11","2","Healthcare and Long-Term Care Expenditure Reform","continue addressing ongoing reforms to restrain the rising trend of healthcare and long-term care expenditures as a percentage of GDP",""],[1,"11","2","Backcasting-Based Economic and Fiscal Management","We will backcast from the long-term goals described above when proceeding with mid-term economic and fiscal management.",""],[1,"13","1","Intergenerational Social Security Benefit Reform","we will revise benefit and burden structures between active and elderly generations through adherence to the principle of ability to pay",""],[1,"13","1","Sustainable Healthcare and Caregiving System Reform","achieve an efficient and resilient healthcare and caregiving system that earns the confidence of the people",""]],"59":[[1,"3","10","Social Innovation Investment and Technology Implementation","increasing investment and implementing innovative technologies in society",""],[1,"4","2","Startup Network Development","building startup networks",""],[1,"4","3","Startup Support and Network Development","Supporting startups and building their networks",""],[1,"4","3","EXPO 2025 Osaka Kansai Promotion","Promoting the EXPO 2025 OSAKA, KANSAI, JAPAN",""],[1,"6","4","Growth-Area Investment for Productivity Enhancement","Companies could use the increased profits as capital to further invest in growth areas, thereby enhancing their productivity and earning power.",""],[1,"7","1","Strategic Growth-Area Investment Programme","Strategic investments should be promptly made, with a long-term perspective, in fields such as green initiatives, digital transformation, science and technology innovation, frontier exploration, and economic and energy security, among others.",""],[1,"8","1","Digital Technology Implementation Initiative","implement digital technologies",""],[1,"8","1","Space and Ocean Frontier Exploration Programme","explore new frontiers like space and oceans",""],[1,"8","1","Domestic Investment Expansion in Growth Sectors","sustainably expand domestic investment in growth sectors",""],[1,"8","3","Structural Competitiveness and Growth Reforms","The government will implement structural reforms to enhance competitiveness and growth potential",""],[1,"9","2","DX and GX Investment Expansion","expanding investments such as DX and GX initiatives",""],[1,"9","2","National Productivity Enhancement Measures","raising productivity to levels comparable to those in Europe and the United States",""],[1,"9","4","Digital Transformation and Frontier Innovation Promotion","we will promote innovation through the widespread social implementation of DX and new technologies as well as the development of frontiers",""],[1,"10","1","Growth Sector Talent and Capital Mobilization","We will channel talent and capital into growth sectors to enhance productivity and increase supply capacity.",""],[1,"10","1","Next-Generation Technology Market Creation","Additionally, we will create and expand new markets by generating high-value solutions using next-generation technologies and new business models, thereby fostering an economic structure driven by private-sector demand.",""],[1,"10","1","Public-Private Domestic Investment Expansion","both the public and private sectors should be more active in increasing domestic investment, thereby shifting the corporate sector from a surplus of savings to a surplus of investments.",""],[1,"10","1","New Player Innovation Ecosystem","Additionally, we will create an ecosystem that supports the activities of new players, including startups engaged in the social implementation of new technologies, as well as social businesses and NGOs.",""],[1,"12","4","Research and Development Investment","research and development",""],[1,"12","4","Corporate Rejuvenation Promotion","promoting corporate rejuvenation",""],[1,"12","4","Societal Technology Matching Opportunities","expanding opportunities to match societal issues with new technologies",""],[1,"12","4","Comprehensive Startup Support","providing startups with comprehensive support through government procurement and regulatory reforms",""],[1,"13","1","Public-Private Future Growth Investment Programme","promote investments in sectors crucial for future growth under medium- and long-term plans through cooperation between the public and private sectors",""],[1,"20","8","Growth Market Entry and Business Transformation Initiatives","The government will promote initiatives for companies aiming to enter growth markets, including business restructuring, development of new products and exploration of new markets, innovation creation, DX and GX.",""],[1,"20","6","Open Innovation Partnerships for New Technology Development","The government will encourage large enterprises to engage in developing new technologies and products in collaboration with LMEs and SMEs (open innovation)",""]],"60":[[1,"4","3","Local Community Revitalization and Local Initiatives","Responding to social challenges through local community revitalization and local initiatives",""],[1,"11","4","Regional Revitalization and Community Development","regional revitalization efforts to address population decline and Tokyo-centric concentration, addressing natural and societal population decreases and foster autonomous local communities that capitalize on regional characteristics and attractiveness",""],[1,"11","4","Intermunicipal Public Service and Infrastructure Coordination","promote efforts for local municipalities to collaboratively provide public services and maintain infrastructure across wider areas",""],[1,"11","4","Municipal Digital Transformation and Technology Support","assisting them in implementing digital transformation (DX) and new technologies to offer more sophisticated functions and services",""],[1,"13","1","Regional Model Area Technology and Regulatory Initiative","we will establish model regions, where, through regulatory and institutional reforms, as well as coordination among policies and regions, we will pursue pioneering initiatives, before expanding them horizontally across other regions",""],[1,"13","1","Compact Urban Area Restructuring","we will gather residents' opinions to restructure large urban areas into more compact forms based on these inputs",""],[1,"13","1","Regional Revitalization and Interregional Cooperation","rectify Tokyo-centric concentration to build a more resilient national land structure while enhancing local fiscal foundations mainly through revitalizing regional economies, promoting cooperation and coordination across broad regions",""],[1,"22","1","Industrial Infrastructure Utilization and Resilience Investment","The government will work on the effective utilization, development, and resilience of infrastructure such as industrial water supply and industrial land.",""],[1,"22","1","Collaborative Vision for Local Economy Enterprises","We will formulate a vision in which relevant ministries collaborate for LMEs that drive the local economy and small enterprises aiming to grow their sales to over 10 billion yen.",""],[1,"22","1","Local Enterprise Support Assistance System","Additionally, we will establish a system in which local governments and support agencies assist these enterprises.",""],[1,"22","3","Local Challenge Demonstration Project Support","will support demonstration projects based on the Basic Policy for Promoting Business to Solve Local Challenges Formulated19.",""],[1,"22","3","Business Model and Social Impact Assessment Method Development","we will organize business models and establish methods for support and social impact assessment.",""]],"61":[[1,"4","1","Promotion of Japan as a Leading Asset Management Center","Promoting Japan as a Leading Asset Management Center",""],[1,"4","2","Overseas Connectivity Improvement","improving connectivity overseas",""],[1,"4","3","Overseas Economic Engagement Initiative","Leveraging overseas vitality",""],[1,"8","1","Overseas Human and Financial Resource Mobilization Mechanism","attract human and financial resources from overseas",""],[1,"12","2","International Market Connectivity Enhancement","the government will enhance Japan's connectivity with growing markets",""],[1,"12","2","Overseas Human and Financial Resource Attraction","actively attract human and financial resources from overseas",""],[1,"13","1","Global South Market Expansion Strategy","we will fundamentally strengthen our global strategy from the perspectives of goods, capital, and people",""],[1,"7","4","SME Overseas Expansion Support","support SMEs in their initiatives to ... pursue overseas expansion",""],[1,"22","5","External Demand Capture Support for LMEs and SMEs","The government will encourage and support LMEs and SMEs in undertaking ambitious efforts to capture external demand.",""],[1,"22","6","Expert Accompanied Support for New Exporters","the government will enhance tailored support for these businesses by strengthening the accompanied support system of experts",""],[1,"22","6","Expansion of Overseas Export Support Bases","adding overseas bases",""],[1,"22","6","Domestic Systems for Overseas Market Intelligence","enhancing domestic systems to support the understanding of local needs and the formulation of overseas business strategies",""],[1,"22","6","Export-Oriented Product Development Support","supporting the development of products that meet the demands of overseas markets",""],[1,"22","6","Continuous Export Escort Support","we will work to provide continuous support from who provide assistance as escort runner",""],[1,"22","6","JETRO Overseas E-Commerce Expansion","expand overseas e-commerce sites centrally contracted by JETRO to offer sales opportunities to SMEs",""],[1,"22","6","English Communication Skills Support for Exporters","support the improvement of English communication skills for business operators",""],[1,"22","6","Export Partnership Coordination Mechanism","strengthen collaboration between the Organization for Small & Medium Enterprises and Regional Innovation, Japan (SME Support, Japan) and export trading companies and/or platforms, etc.",""],[1,"22","7","Local Company Overseas Expansion Support Initiative","The government will encourage local trading companies and companies with digital technologies that play a central role in supporting the overseas expansion of",""]],"62":[[1,"23","7","Web3 Token Use and Payment Facilitation Policy","promoting the efficient use of tokens and facilitating smooth payments based on web3-related technologies (including NFTs 23 based on blockchain technology)",""],[1,"23","7","Content Industry Revitalization Environment","enhancing the environment to revitalize the content industry",""],[1,"23","7","Web3 Use Case Creation Support","supporting the creation of use cases",""],[1,"23","8","Mobile Software Competition Act Implementation","To swiftly and effectively implement the Mobile Software Competition Act",""],[1,"24","1","Japan Fair Trade Commission Capacity Enhancement","the government will drastically enhance the Japan Fair Trade Commission's framework in terms of both quality and quantity, particularly by promoting the appointment of advanced digital specialists.","Japan Fair Trade Commission"],[1,"24","2","Mobile Phone Market Competition Policy","promote fair competition in the mobile phone market",""],[1,"24","3","Central Bank Digital Currency Introduction Study","the government and the Bank of Japan deepen discussions based on the interim report 25, taking into account international trends to clearly identify the basic considerations on main issues and possible options for the introduction of a CBDC, outlining its design. Afterward, we will consider the feasibility and legal aspects of issuing a CBDC.",""]],"63":[[1,"24","4","Artificial Intelligence Research and Data Development Programme","we will strengthen research and development capabilities, including data development",""],[1,"24","4","Artificial Intelligence Utilization Promotion Initiative","promote AI utilization",""],[1,"24","4","Artificial Intelligence Computing Infrastructure Upgrade","upgrade infrastructure to accommodate expansion and complexity of computing resources",""],[1,"24","4","Artificial Intelligence Skills Development and Information Management Programme","develop and recruiting skilled workers by managing skill information of individuals",""],[1,"24","4","Voluntary Artificial Intelligence Business Guidelines","businesses engage voluntarily in initiatives based on the AI Guidelines for Business",""],[1,"24","4","Artificial Intelligence Regulatory Guardrails and Safety Evaluation","advancing the evaluation of regulatory frameworks as guardrails and safety of AI",""],[1,"24","4","Artificial Intelligence Disinformation Countermeasures","measures to combat disinformation and misinformation",""],[1,"24","4","Artificial Intelligence Intellectual Property Response Measures","responses to issues related to intellectual property rights and others",""],[1,"24","4","International Artificial Intelligence Rule-Making Collaboration","the government will take a leading role in international collaboration and coordination in rule-making",""],[1,"24","5","AI and Semiconductor Investment Support Programme","To this end, the government, while securing the necessary financial resources, will focus on providing substantial and planned investment support over multiple fiscal years for mass production investments and research and development in these fields.",""],[1,"24","5","Legislative Measures for Next-Generation Semiconductor Mass Production","we will consider the necessary legislative measures especially for the mass production of next-generation",""],[1,"25","1","Semiconductor Investment and Loan Support Diversification","we will explore diversifying support methods, including the expansion of utilization of necessary investments and loans.",""]],"64":[[1,"26","3","Digital Vaccination Procedure Improvement","the government will aim to improve efficiency of vaccination procedures through digitalization",""],[1,"26","3","Digital Adverse Vaccination Reaction Reporting","promoting online reports of suspected adverse reactions after vaccination",""],[1,"26","3","Vaccination Database Establishment","establishing a vaccination database",""]],"65":[[1,"8","1","Public-Private Collaboration for Green Transformation and Economic Security","through public-private collaboration to solve social issues such as GX and economic security",""],[1,"29","3","GX-Related Investment Promotion","the government will promote over 150 trillion yen in GX-related investments over the next decade, in collaboration between the public sector and the private sector, based on the goals of achieving net-zero by 2050 and reducing greenhouse gas emissions by 46% in FY 2030 (compared to FY 2013 levels).",""],[1,"29","3","National GX Strategy Formulation","Additionally, by the end of FY 2024, the government will formulate the national strategy for GX and revise the Strategic Energy Plan and the Plan for Global Warming Countermeasures.",""],[1,"29","3","Strategic Energy and Climate Plan Revision","Additionally, by the end of FY 2024, the government will formulate the national strategy for GX and revise the Strategic Energy Plan and the Plan for Global Warming Countermeasures.",""],[1,"31","3","Pro-Growth Carbon Pricing Scheme","The government will work towards the realization and implementation of the Pro-Growth Carbon Pricing Scheme 44 in accordance with the Sector-specific Investment Strategies for GX.",""],[1,"31","4","Synthetic Methane CO2 Emissions Accounting Framework","The government will examine the principles for calculating CO2 emissions when consuming synthetic methane and aim to reach a conclusion by the end of fiscal year 2024.",""],[1,"31","4","Carbon Dioxide Storage Business Act","The Act Concerning Carbon Dioxide Storage Business (Act No. 38 of 2024).",""]],"66":[[1,"9","3","Backcasting-Based Institutional Reform Initiative","will use backcasting from the Five Visions for Advancing to a New Stage stated below to implement intensive efforts, including necessary institutional reforms, in principle over the next three years.",""],[1,"11","4","Declining Birthrate Countermeasures","the government will unite to vigorously promote measures to halt the rapid national population decline through countermeasures against declining birthrates",""],[1,"14","2","Intergenerational Community Dialogue Mechanism","individuals, organizations, and local communities engage in discussions spanning generations to widely share the inevitable challenges posed by Japan's declining population and the vision to resolve them",""],[1,"14","2","Citizen Engagement and Public Awareness Movement","fostering a transformation of public awareness and igniting a movement that engages citizens are essential",""],[1,"14","2","Policy Communication and Cross-Ministry Implementation Mechanism","we will actively communicate the fundamental ideas and policy approaches for our medium- to long-term policy management outlined in this Basic Policy, collaborating with relevant ministries and agencies to ensure effective implementation",""],[1,"29","1","Public and Private Systems Linkage Mechanism","the linkage of various public and private systems35.",""],[1,"16","5","Environmental Improvements for Primary Industries","the government will advance environmental improvements aimed at increasing their",""]],"67":[[1,"31","4","GX Investment Incentive and Carbon Pricing Mechanism","The concept of accelerating GX investment by providing incentives for upfront investments through the use of GX Economy Transition Bond, etc. and carbon pricing.",""],[1,"32","1","GX Economy Transition Bond Financing","backed by GX Economy Transition Bond45",""],[1,"32","1","Carbon Pricing System Establishment","designing and establishing systems for carbon pricing46",""],[1,"32","1","Private Finance Mobilization through GX Acceleration Agency","attracting private funds through the GX Acceleration Agency",""],[1,"32","1","Asian Transition Finance Collaboration","promoting transition finance 47 in collaboration with countries in Asia",""],[1,"32","1","Green Finance Advancement","advancing green finance48",""],[1,"32","1","Sustainable Finance Enabling Environment","establishing an environment to promote sustainable finance49",""],[1,"32","6","GX Strategic Sector Tax Legislation","the government plans to submit the necessary legislation for measures related to materials included in the GX sector under the Tax System for Promoting Domestic Production in Strategic Sectors to the regular Diet session in 2025.",""],[1,"32","6","Emissions Trading System","The goal is to start the full-scale operation of the Emissions Trading System by FY 2026",""],[1,"32","6","Fossil Fuel Levy","introduce the Fossil Fuel Levy by FY 2028",""],[1,"32","6","Paid Auctions for Emissions Allowances","begin the phased introduction of Paid Auctions from FY 2033.",""],[1,"32","6","Transition Technology Emissions Reduction Financing","A new financing method to support companies that achieve steady reductions in greenhouse gas emissions through the adoption of technologies in the transition phase.",""],[1,"32","6","Environmentally Conscious Initiative Financing","A financing method specialized for environmentally conscious initiatives, such as measures against global warming and renewable energy projects.",""],[1,"32","6","Sustainability Financial Disclosure Standards","the government will, for example, advance discussions on disclosure and assurance of sustainability-related financial information and contribute to international discussions on the development of disclosure standards related to human capital, including experts in climate change response.",""],[1,"32","6","Joint Crediting Mechanism Promotion","Including the promotion of the Joint Crediting Mechanism (JCM).",""],[1,"33","1","Transition Finance Promotion Mechanism","the promotion of transition finance in collaboration with financial authorities in Asia and private financial institutions54.",""]],"68":[[1,"32","2","Local Decarbonization Leading Areas Programme","the government will designate over 100 decarbonization leading areas by FY 2025 and horizontally deploy advanced initiatives there to revitalize local economies.",""],[1,"32","2","Urban and Port Infrastructure Decarbonization","In addition to infrastructure such as urban development GX, Carbon Neutral Ports, and buildings52, we will advance decarbonization in mobility-related fields, such as fuel cell railway vehicles, zero-emission ships, and next-generation aircraft.",""],[1,"32","2","Low-Carbon Mobility Technology Deployment","we will advance decarbonization in mobility-related fields, such as fuel cell railway vehicles, zero-emission ships, and next-generation aircraft.",""],[1,"32","5","Asia Zero Emission Community Cooperation Initiative","To realize the Asia Zero Emission Community (AZEC) Initiative, the government will contribute to global decarbonization by leveraging Japan’s technologies and systems through bilateral and multilateral cooperation",""],[1,"32","6","Citizen Net-Zero Behavior Change Movement","New national movements to facilitate behavior change and lifestyle transformation among citizens, aiming to achieve net-zero by 2050.",""],[1,"32","6","Lifecycle Building CO2 Reduction Initiative","An initiative to promote the reduction of CO2 emissions from buildings throughout their entire lifecycle, from construction to demolition.",""],[1,"39","5","Country-Tailored Decarbonization Cooperation and Technology Assistance","In priority areas such as decarbonization, this type of cooperation is aimed at realizing development goals together through proposals for assistance suitable for each country and dialogue with partner countries.",""],[1,"46","4","Okinawa Decarbonization Measures","decarbonization",""]],"69":[[1,"35","3","DX High School Project","We will continuously implement initiatives such as the DX High School Project to promote exploratory, interdisciplinary, and practical learning and enhance science and mathematics education",""],[1,"35","3","Primary and Secondary Information Education Enhancement","strengthen and enrich information education 62 at the primary and secondary education levels",""],[1,"35","3","University Faculty Reorganization for Growth Areas","reorganizing university faculties to focus on growth areas",""],[1,"35","3","Internationalization of KOSEN Cutting-Edge Technology Education","advancing and internationalizing college of technology (KOSEN) education in cutting-edge technologies such as semiconductors",""],[1,"35","3","Internationalization of Education and English Learning","we will advance the internationalization of education63, including enhancing English education and international exchanges such as the use of AI",""],[1,"35","3","New Tobitate Young Ambassador Program Expansion and Financial Support","consider expanding the New Tobitate Young Ambassador Program and providing financial support for",""],[1,"35","4","Statistical Experts Development Programme","Including the development of statistical experts.",""],[1,"35","4","International Expansion of Japanese-Style Educational Methods","Including the international expansion of Japanese-style educational methods.",""],[1,"36","1","International Doctoral Study Programme","sending them to top-tier universities' doctoral programs in science fields",""],[1,"36","1","Public-Private Cooperation in Overseas Education","cooperation between the public and private sectors",""],[1,"36","1","Overseas Educational Facilities Enhancement","enhance the distinctive educational activities of the Overseas Educational Facilities",""],[1,"36","1","Industry-Academia-Government Co-Creation Initiative","promote co-creation among industry, academia, and government",""],[1,"36","1","Graduate School Reform for Economic and Societal Needs","undertake initiatives to reform graduate schools in response to economic and societal needs",""],[1,"36","1","Doctoral Graduate Career Opportunities and Treatment Improvement","create opportunities for doctoral graduates to play active roles in various fields (including government agencies), and improve their treatment",""],[1,"36","1","Recurrent Education and Reskilling Ecosystem","accelerate efforts to create a recurrent education ecosystem involving industry, individuals, and educational institutions",""]],"70":[[1,"40","4","Content Industry Revitalization Strategy","The government will promote the Content Industry Revitalization Strategy77 for anime, music, broadcast programs, movies, games, manga, etc., through public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"40","5","Content Industry Public-Private Council","The government will establish the Content Industry Public-Private Council77 and the Film Strategic Planning Committee77 as its control towers, respectively, and integrate relevant measures from the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology and the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry into the Creator Support Fund in order to provide consistent and strong support.",""],[1,"40","5","Film Strategic Planning Committee","The government will establish the Content Industry Public-Private Council77 and the Film Strategic Planning Committee77 as its control towers, respectively, and integrate relevant measures from the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology and the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry into the Creator Support Fund in order to provide consistent and strong support.",""],[1,"40","5","Creator Support Fund Measure Integration","The government will establish the Content Industry Public-Private Council77 and the Film Strategic Planning Committee77 as its control towers, respectively, and integrate relevant measures from the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology and the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry into the Creator Support Fund in order to provide consistent and strong support.","Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology | Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry"],[1,"40","6","Content Industry Overseas Expansion Support","we will support overseas expansion of",""],[1,"41","1","Creative Industry International Promotion Support","production companies, such as by exhibiting at international trade fairs and film festivals",""],[1,"41","1","Study-Abroad Support for Aspiring Creators","will provide study-abroad support for students and others aiming to become creators",""],[1,"41","2","Self-Financed Video Production Support","The government will support production companies that raise their own funds for the production of their works",""],[1,"41","2","International Large-Scale Video Production Attraction","encourage overseas production companies to shoot large-scale video works on locations in Japan using advanced digital technologies such as VFX78.",""],[1,"41","3","Content Industry Work Environment and Wage Improvement","The government will develop a proper work environment for production sites and further improve the relevant environment in terms of wage payment so that creators in the content industry can continuously work with peace in mind.",""],[1,"41","3","Creator Transaction Survey","The Japan Fair Trade Commission and other relevant ministries and agencies will cooperate to conduct a survey or surveys of transactions between performers and their offices in the field of music and broadcast programs by the end of 2024","Japan Fair Trade Commission"],[1,"41","3","Guidelines for Optimizing Creator Transactions","based on the results of the survey(s), start drafting guidelines for the optimization of transactions relevant to creators.","Japan Fair Trade Commission"],[1,"41","4","Web3 Business Model Development Support","support the construction of business models utilizing new technologies such as web3",""],[1,"41","4","Creator Discovery Support Programme","support the discovery of excellent creators",""],[1,"41","4","Production and Management Personnel Development Programme","nurture production and management personnel",""],[1,"41","4","Anti-Piracy Measures","work on measures against pirated editions",""]],"71":[[1,"42","2","EXPO 2025 Osaka-Kansai Preparation and Management Programme","In preparation for the opening of EXPO 2025 OSAKA, KANSAI, which is a laboratory for a future society, the government will ensure the proper participation/exhibition of various countries/international organizations, the construction of venues, and security, including disaster response, and will properly execute and manage the relevant budgets.",""],[1,"42","2","Future Society Technology Demonstration and Dissemination Initiative","We will also demonstrate, implement, and disseminate technologies that will solve social issues such as mobility, energy/environment, digital, life science, and space under the theme of “Designing a Future Society for Our Lives.”",""],[1,"42","2","National Expo Exchange and Engagement Initiative","The government will work on building momentum across the country by, for example, having children and youths in Japan and Expo participant countries engage in exchanges.",""],[1,"42","2","Expo Visitor Attraction to Rural Areas Initiative","We will work to attract Expo visitors to the countryside.",""],[1,"42","3","International Horticultural Expo 2027 Preparation","We will steadily prepare for the International Horticultural Expo 2027, Yokohama, Japan.",""]],"72":[[1,"42","4","Local Technology-Based Social Problem-Solving Initiative","we need to thoroughly utilize new technologies to solve local social issues",""],[1,"42","4","Attractive Local Communities Initiative for Women and Youth","the government will strongly support local initiatives such as the creation of an attractive community for women and young people, including accompanying support",""],[1,"43","1","Digital Technology-Enabled Local Community Revitalization","accelerating local community revitalization by utilizing the power of digital technology",""],[1,"43","1","Regional Living Areas for Sustainable Daily Services","the government will promote the formation of regional living areas where services necessary for daily life are provided on a sustainable basis regardless of administrative districts",""],[1,"43","1","Decentralized Nation Development","the creation of a decentralized nation that is mutually beneficial to the regions and Tokyo",""],[1,"43","1","Digital Garden City Nation Land Formation Vision","will develop the Vision for a Digital Garden City Nation into national land formation",""],[1,"43","2","Digital Garden City Institutional and Regulatory Reform Support","the government will package and support institutional and regulatory reforms",""],[1,"43","2","Inter-Policy and Inter-Regional Digital Partnerships","the government will package and support ... inter-policy and inter-regional partnerships",""],[1,"43","2","Digital Garden City Initiative Grant Support","the prioritization of support for effective initiatives through grants for the Vision for a Digital Garden City Nation",""],[1,"43","2","Special Zones for Digital Community Innovation","while utilizing Super Cities, Digital Garden Health Special Zones, and “Kizuna” Special Zones for Cooperation, etc.",""],[1,"43","2","Lateral Deployment of Digital Service Systems","We will promote effective and efficient lateral deployment of service systems that support good practices such as 5G utilization",""],[1,"43","2","Nationwide Digital Infrastructure Development","development of digital infrastructure such as optical fiber, 5G, and data centers nationwide",""],[1,"43","2","Digital Human Resources Development Programme","development of digital human resources",""],[1,"43","3","Digital Administrative and Fiscal Reform for Public Services","In view of the rapid decline in population, etc., the government will review appropriate modus of the administrative and fiscal conditions at the user's point of view, and implement measures based on the Report of Digital Administrative and Fiscal Reform 2024 81 to realize the maintenance and enhancement of public services, etc., by making the best use of digital.",""],[1,"44","2","National-Local Digital Services Liaison System","we will put into place a liaison and consultation system between the national and local governments this summer so that they can use common digital services.",""],[1,"44","2","Common Digital Government Infrastructure Development","ministries and agencies will work together with the Digital Agency and the Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications to proactively review operations and build systems, and will promote initial development, transition and dissemination support, development of digital public infrastructure such as Base Registry, and dissemination support to local governments","Digital Agency | Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications"],[1,"44","2","Public Service DX Regional Hub Network","we will form a hub function for promoting the public service DX in each prefecture, and the respective prefectures will support the local governments in their regions",""],[1,"44","2","Digital Government Specialist Recruitment Support","the national government will support the recruitment of specialized human resources.",""],[1,"44","2","Government Information System Expense Visualization","the government will improve efficiency by visualizing the information system expenses of each government agency.",""],[1,"44","2","Policy Progress Monitoring and Logic Model System","the government will monitor and improve policy progress by setting medium- and long-term KPIs and building logic models, etc.",""],[1,"44","2","Fund Review and Evidence-Based Budget Management","we will continue to review the Fund as a whole and promote PDCA initiatives based on the EBPM approach, including the return of surplus funds to the national treasury and improvement of performance targets from the viewpoint of effective utilization of the Fund.",""],[1,"44","2","Administrative Review and Budget Coordination Reform","the government will strengthen the coordination between the review of administrative projects and the budget for the entire budget projects and promote systematization and openness.",""]],"73":[[1,"43","4","Regulatory and Service System Reform for Autonomous Mobility","the government will review regulations and systems and develop systems to improve the sustainability and convenience of services such as the social implementation of autonomous driving.",""],[1,"43","4","Nationwide Ride-Sharing Expansion","we will make so-called ride-sharing widely available nationwide on the premise of safety, from the viewpoint of using digital technology, to lay the path for solving the shortage of mobility nationwide.",""],[1,"43","4","Private Car Utilization Project Monitoring and Verification","the government will carry out monitoring and verification of the private car utilization project and the like, so as to evaluate the verification results at each point in time.",""],[1,"43","4","Legal Framework for Non-Taxi Ride-Sharing Operators","we will discuss an appropriate modus of the ride-sharing project to be conducted by persons other than taxi operators, including the relevant legal system",""],[1,"44","5","Compact Plus Network Regional Consolidation and Connectivity Initiative","the government will deepen and develop the initiatives of the Compact Plus Network by promoting the formation of the consolidation bases of various service functions and regional life zones, as well as by strengthening the connection of the entire national land.",""],[1,"45","1","Local Public Transportation Redesign","the government will accelerate the redesigning initiatives87 such as transportation DX and GX, cooperation and collaboration with various stakeholders, reconstruction of local railways, activation of route buses, and utilization of local private cars and general drivers, including private paid passenger transportation, to promote labor saving, and to secure personnel in charge.",""],[1,"45","3","Local Public Transportation Redesign","Realization for Redesigning Local Public Transportation",""],[1,"45","1","Trunk Railway Function Enhancement","we will make further efforts to enhance the functionality of trunk railways in accordance with local circumstances",""],[1,"45","2","Logistics and People-Flow Network Development","the government will work on the early development and utilization of logistics and people-flow networks such as high-standard roads, new shinkansen lines 88, Linear Chuo Shinkansen, urban railways, ports and airports",""],[1,"45","2","Transport Modal Connection Strengthening","the strengthening of modal connections",""],[1,"45","2","Aviation and Maritime Network Activation","the maintenance and activation of aviation and maritime networks",""],[1,"45","2","Shipbuilding and Shipping Competitiveness Strengthening","the strengthening of competitiveness in the shipbuilding and shipping industries",""],[1,"45","2","Transport Sector Personnel Development","the securing and nurturing of personnel in charge",""],[1,"45","2","Transport Network Planning Research","we will also conduct research and studies on various issues, including the direction, in accordance with the actual situation of the basic planned routes and trunk railway networks",""],[1,"45","2","Linear Chuo Shinkansen Environmental and Financial Monitoring","the government will strictly monitor the status of the environment and water resources as well as the financial conditions of construction entities",""],[1,"45","2","Linear Chuo Shinkansen Implementation Guidance and Technical Support","provide necessary guidance and technical support so that the development of the line can proceed appropriately under the current assumed timing for the opening of the entire line89",""],[1,"45","3","School Route Traffic Safety Measures","traffic safety measures for school routes and others",""],[1,"45","3","Bicycle Use Promotion Initiative","promotion of the use of bicycles",""],[1,"45","3","Unstarted Transport Section Development","necessary studies are being carried out, and we will further work on the early development of the sections where construction has not yet started",""],[1,"46","1","Station Area Community Development Initiative","we will promote the community development, including the area around stations in cooperation with local governments along the line, by for example, deepening reviews of the stations90 from Nagoya to the west.",""],[1,"46","1","Surplus Shinkansen Capacity Utilization Initiative","improving convenience in the region by utilizing the surplus transportation capacity of the Tokaido Shinkansen.",""],[1,"46","2","Logistics Base and Network Function Strengthening","strengthening the functions of logistics bases and networks",""],[1,"46","2","Modal Shift for Logistics Efficiency","improving efficiency through modal shifts",""],[1,"46","2","Logistics DX and Standardization Initiative","logistics DX and standardization",""],[1,"46","2","Logistics Business Practice Rectification Reform","rectifying business practices",""],[1,"46","2","Shipper and Consumer Behavior Change Initiative","changing the behavior of shippers and consumers",""],[1,"46","2","Revised Logistics Act Enforcement System","establishing an enforcement system for the revised Logistics Act",""],[1,"46","5","Tokyo–Osaka High-Speed Rail Opening Acceleration","for the opening between Tokyo and Osaka by up to eight years (2037 at the earliest) from the initial target of 2045.",""]],"74":[[1,"46","4","Tourism Quality Improvement Measures","improving the quality of tourism",""],[1,"47","5","Inbound Tourism Experience Development","the government will promote the provision of special experiences",""],[1,"47","5","Local Tourism Content Development","the creation of diverse local tourism content such as adventure tourism",""],[1,"47","5","Tourism Human Resources Development","the development of human resources for tourism, including local guides",""],[1,"47","5","Luxury Inbound Tourism Destination Development","creating luxury inbound tourist destinations",""],[1,"47","5","National Park and Public Facility Attractiveness Improvement","the improvement of the attractiveness of national parks, quasi-national parks, national gardens, and public facilities",""],[1,"47","5","Inbound Tourism Reception Environment Development","the development of reception environments for airports, CIQs, and secondary transportation",""],[1,"47","5","Cruise Tourism and Hub Development","revival of cruises and cruise hub formation",""],[1,"47","5","Tourism Consumption Tax Exemption Reform","the review and proper use of the consumption tax exemption system",""],[1,"47","5","Traditional Sake-Making Knowledge Promotion","the strategic promotion, the dissemination of attractiveness of traditional knowledge and skills of sake-making with koji mold in Japan",""],[1,"47","5","MICE Attraction and Hosting","the attraction and holding of MICE",""],[1,"47","5","Integrated Resort Development and Casino Regulation","the development of integrated resorts (IR), including strict casino regulations",""],[1,"47","5","Digital Nomad Visa Promotion","the promotion of the use of digital nomad visas",""],[1,"47","5","Outbound Tourism and International Exchange Expansion","the expansion of outbound and international exchanges",""],[1,"47","6","Sustainable Tourism Facility Renovation Initiative","With the aim of improving sustainable tourism regions, the government will encourage the renovation, etc., of accommodation facilities and tourist facilities",""],[1,"48","1","Tourism Destination and Industry Value Enhancement","promote revitalizing and adding high-value to tourist destinations and the tourism industry.",""],[1,"48","1","Tourism Labor Efficiency and Workforce Support","The government will take comprehensive measures to counter the shortage of human resources by improving the efficiency and labor saving of business in tourism DX, tourist destinations and the tourism industry, and utilizing foreign nationals.",""],[1,"48","1","Overtourism Management Measures","The government will promote taking measures against overtourism",""],[1,"48","1","Tourist Destination Management Systems","the establishment of management systems for tourist destinations.",""],[1,"48","2","Domestic Exchange and Inclusive Tourism Promotion","With the aim of expanding domestic exchanges, the government will promote WORKATION, universal tourism, and other measures so as to level demand and expand new exchange markets.",""]],"75":[[1,"48","4","Agricultural Basic Plan Revision","the government will revise the Basic Plan100 by the end of FY 2024.",""],[1,"48","4","Agricultural Structural Transformation Support System","the government will enhance and strengthen measures and secure a system to ensure that the structural transformation of agriculture can be promoted intensively in the first five years",""],[1,"48","5","Food Self-Sufficiency Target-Setting Framework","the government will set new targets including the food self-sufficiency ratio and other indexes",""],[1,"48","5","Agricultural and Food Production Base Strengthening","strengthen the production base of agriculture, forestry, fisheries and the food industry",""],[1,"48","5","Domestic Food and Production Material Expansion","promote structural changes such as the expansion of domestic productivity of food and production materials that are highly dependent on imports101, including the conversion of paddy fields into multipurpose paddy fields and upland fields",""],[1,"48","5","Food Import and Stockpile Stability Mechanism","while ensuring stable imports and stockpiles",""],[1,"48","5","Agricultural, Forestry and Fishery Export Promotion","We will promote the export of agricultural, forestry and fishery products and foods in response to overseas demand",""],[1,"48","5","Food Supply Difficulty Preparedness Policies","formulating basic policies to prepare for food supply difficulties",""],[1,"48","5","Sustainable Food System Cost and Pricing Reform","the government will proceed with consultations on the preparation of cost indicators, aiming to submit to the next ordinary Diet session a bill on the relevant legal system to ensure the sustainability of the food system, including institutionalization of the formation of reasonable food prices",""],[1,"48","5","Food Access Support for Grocery-Inaccessible People","In order to facilitate the provision of food to people who have difficulty accessing grocery stores",""],[1,"49","1","Food Access Support Initiatives for Impoverished Children","the government will promote initiatives in line with the Package of Support Measures for Ensuring Food Access102.",""],[1,"49","2","Agricultural Cross-Compliance Environmental Standards","implementing cross-compliance",""],[1,"49","2","Support for Organic Agriculture Initiatives","supporting advanced initiatives103 such as organic agriculture",""],[1,"49","3","Regional Agricultural Personnel Development Programme","the government will promote the development and securing of personnel in charge based on regional plans",""],[1,"49","3","Agricultural Land Consolidation and Intensification","the agglomeration and intensification of agricultural land",""],[1,"49","3","Agricultural Land Improvement Projects","land improvement projects",""],[1,"49","3","Agricultural Service Business Development","the development and activities of service business entities",""],[1,"49","3","Agricultural Land Security and Effective Use Measures","the securing and proper and effective use of total agricultural land",""],[1,"49","3","Agricultural Corporation Management Strengthening","the strengthening of the management base of agricultural corporations in cooperation with the food industry",""],[1,"49","3","Smart Agriculture Technology Deployment","the development of smart technologies and the conversion of production methods and the acceleration of the implementation of these technologies",""],[1,"49","3","Agricultural Management Stabilization Measures","management stabilization measures",""],[1,"49","3","Livestock Disease Control Programme","livestock disease control",""],[1,"49","3","Women’s Participation in Agriculture Initiative","the promotion of women's participation",""],[1,"49","3","Irrigation and Drainage Facility Conservation Legislation","the government will also aim to submit legislation on land improvement for the appropriate conservation and management of irrigation drainage facilities, etc., to the next ordinary Diet session",""],[1,"49","3","Hilly and Mountainous Agricultural Land Conservation","the conservation and the measures against the extensive use of agricultural land in hilly and mountainous areas",""],[1,"49","3","Rural Local Industry Promotion Initiative","the promotion of local industries that contribute to the increase in the number of people involved in rural areas",""],[1,"49","3","Agriculture and Welfare Collaboration Initiative","agriculture and welfare collaboration",""],[1,"49","3","Wildlife Nuisance Mitigation Measures","measures to combat wildlife nuisance",""],[1,"49","3","Rice Terrace Promotion Initiative","the promotion of rice terraces",""],[1,"49","6","Mobile Food Catering Access Initiative","This includes the introduction of mobile catering vehicles",""],[1,"49","6","Food Bank and Children's Cafeteria Support","the support for food banks and children's cafeterias",""],[1,"49","6","Urban Agriculture Promotion Initiative","the government will promote urban agriculture, which will also contribute to improving food access",""],[1,"49","6","Environmental Burden Reduction Subsidy System","The government is considering the establishment of a system around fiscal 2027 to provide subsidies for advanced initiatives to reduce the environmental burden.",""]],"76":[[1,"50","3","Lifetime Support Provider Guidelines Dissemination","the government will continue to disseminate the guidelines for lifetime support providers for the elderly and the like",""],[1,"50","3","Cross-Government Support for Elderly People Living Alone","the government will continue to promote cross-government measures for the elderly living alone and the like, such as examining ways to provide necessary support, including information registration platforms.",""],[1,"50","3","Dementia Basic Plan and Measures","we will enact the dementia basic plan, and promote dementia measures 106.",""],[1,"50","3","Ageing Society Measures Guideline","the government will formulate a new guideline of measures for ageing society this summer.",""],[1,"50","3","Integrated Self-Reliance Support for Needy Persons","the government will promote the integrated implementation with the self-reliance support system for needy persons in order to create a welfare system that can be used appropriately and that leads to self-reliance.",""],[1,"50","3","Livelihood Assistance Standards Adjustment","With regard to the standards for livelihood assistance, we will take necessary measures based on socioeconomic conditions, etc.",""],[1,"50","3","Housing Support through Safety Net Systems","As for housing support, the government will strengthen the relevant support through the self-reliance support system for needy persons and the housing safety net system.",""],[1,"50","3","Inter-Ministerial Housing Access Environment","the related ministries and agencies will cooperate to promote the development of an environment in which persons requiring special assistance in securing housing can live with peace of mind.",""],[1,"50","3","Universal Design Community Development","the government will promote universal design community development",""],[1,"50","3","Barrier-Free Mindset Initiatives","the government will promote universal design community development and barrier-free mindset initiatives",""],[1,"50","3","Disability Employment and Community Life Support","support the employment and community life of persons with disabilities108 based on the Fifth Term Basic Plan for Persons with Disabilities109",""],[1,"50","3","Lifelong Learning Promotion","promote lifelong learning",""],[1,"50","4","Dementia and Mild Cognitive Impairment Early Detection Initiatives","This includes initiatives based on the results of demonstration projects such as cognitive function tests for early detection and early response of dementia and mild cognitive impairment.",""],[1,"50","4","Support Measures for Persons Blind in One Eye","This includes considering measures to support persons who are blind in one eye while listening to opinions of the persons.",""],[1,"51","1","Multi-tiered Support System Development Projects","municipalities implementing the multi-tiered support system development projects",""],[1,"51","1","Disability Rights and Adult Guardianship Protection","comprehensively protect the rights of persons with disabilities, including adult guardianship systems",""],[1,"51","1","Family Register Inclusion and Resolution Measures","promote the resolution of the problem involving persons without a family register",""],[1,"51","1","Hikikomori Support Programme","The government will steadily promote support for hikikomori (also known as severe social withdrawal)",""],[1,"51","1","Local Youth Support Station Employment System","strengthening the employment support system at local youth support stations",""],[1,"51","1","Sexual Orientation and Gender Identity Understanding Measures","With regard to sexual orientation and gender identity, the government will promote various measures based on the Act on Promoting Public Understanding111",""],[1,"51","1","Animal Welfare and Management Measures","We will promote animal welfare and management.",""],[1,"51","2","Local Public-Private Coordination Platform Establishment Support","backing up local governments at the stage of establishing the local Public-Private Coordination Platforms",""],[1,"51","2","Ongoing Support for NPO Activities","supporting various activities of NPOs and others on an ongoing basis",""],[1,"51","2","Tsunagari Supporters Development Programme","fostering principal supports and those who are interested in those around them, and that they support troubled people where possible (so-called “Tsunagari Supporters”)",""],[1,"51","2","Community Places for Building Social Bonds","creating places where people can build loose bonds from the perspective of preventing states of loneliness and isolation",""],[1,"51","2","Cross-Sectoral Coordination for Social Connections","promoting cross-sectoral coordination to create bonds among people",""],[1,"51","2","Grant and Resource Mobilization for Loneliness Initiatives","while also utilizing grants and other resources",""],[1,"51","3","Employment and Reskilling Support for Middle-Aged and Elderly People","the government will support this generation through measures aimed at middle-aged and elderly people, providing seamless and effective support from consultation and reskilling and upskilling to employment and retention.",""],[1,"51","3","Broad-Based Social Participation Support","In addition, in cooperation with local governments, we will provide broad-based social participation support, including reskilling and upskilling for employment, in accordance with individual circumstances.",""]],"77":[[1,"53","4","Terrorism Prevention Measures","promote measures to prevent terrorism",""],[1,"53","4","Emergency Public Protection Measures","protect the public citizens in the event of an emergency",""],[1,"53","4","ML/TF/PF Counter-Financing Measures","counter Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing, and Proliferation Financing (ML/TF/PF), including efforts through multilateral frameworks.",""],[1,"53","5","Automobile Manufacturer Fraud Prevention Measures","The government will work to prevent fraud by automobile manufacturers, etc.",""],[1,"53","5","Elderly Driver Accident Prevention Measures","prevent accidents by elderly and other drivers",""],[1,"53","5","Automobile Accident Victim Support","support victims of automobile accidents",""],[1,"53","6","Online Fraud Deterrence and Platform Response Measures","The government will strengthen deterrence and response capabilities based on the Comprehensive Measures to Protect People from Frauds, 119 including requiring platform operators to quickly remove and respond to fraud involving fake advertisements impersonating celebrities.",""],[1,"53","7","Sexual Offense Legal Reform Dissemination","thorough dissemination of the content and purpose of the Act for Partial Revision of the Penal Code and the Code of Criminal Procedure (Act No. 66 of 2023), etc. to deal with sexual offenses",""],[1,"53","7","Sexual Victimization Conditions Investigation","steady consideration for prompt implementation of investigations into the actual conditions of sexual victimization, such as the difficulty of reporting victimization",""],[1,"54","1","Online Gambling Illegality Awareness Campaign","to publicize and raise awareness about the illegality of such cases.",""],[1,"54","2","Volunteer Probation Officer Support Programme","enhancing support for volunteer probation officers",""],[1,"54","2","Preventive Justice and Comprehensive Legal Support","enhance preventive justice support functions for issues in Japan and abroad and comprehensive legal support",""],[1,"54","2","Judicial and Bar Examination Digitalization","digitalizing the judicial field and national bar examinations",""],[1,"54","2","Internet Human Rights Protection Measures","take tougher measures to combat human rights violations on the Internet",""],[1,"54","2","Legal Profession Capacity and Law Education Development","improve the personnel and material foundations that should secure legal professionals and promote law related education",""],[1,"54","2","Crime Victim Support Measures","strengthen measures for crime victims, etc.",""],[1,"54","2","International Justice Cooperation and Legal Technical Assistance","the government will promote international cooperation and justice affairs diplomacy under our coordinated diplomatic approach including legal technical cooperation to promote the rule of law",""],[1,"54","2","International Arbitration Promotion Initiative","work to invigorate international arbitration by taking various measures including raising awareness of arbitral institutions in close cooperation between the public and private sectors",""],[1,"54","2","International Legal Human Resources Development","develop international legal human resources",""],[1,"54","2","Foreign-Language Translation of Laws","promote translation of laws and regulations into foreign languages",""],[1,"54","6","Imprisonment Treatment Enhancement Reform","enhancing treatment based on the establishment of imprisonment",""],[1,"54","6","Local Government Cooperation Mechanism","strengthening cooperation with local governments",""]],"78":[[1,"60","3","Wide-Area Evacuation and Acceptance Planning","we will examine the wide-area evacuation and acceptance",""],[1,"60","3","Underground Evacuation Facility Expansion","the government will further secure underground facilities and promote the relevant initiatives",""],[1,"60","3","Civil Protection Mechanism Strengthening","the national and local governments will work together to strengthen its civil protection mechanism",""],[1,"60","3","Comprehensive Maritime Security Initiative","Japan will promote comprehensive maritime security and other initiatives including through Maritime Domain Awareness(MDA) based on the Basic Plan on Ocean Policy",""],[1,"60","3","Coast Guard Patrol Capability Expansion","The Japan Coast Guard will also upgrade and increase the number of patrol vessels and the like, secure operating expenses","The Japan Coast Guard"],[1,"60","3","Unmanned Aircraft for Maritime Security","promote the use of new technologies such as unmanned aircraft","The Japan Coast Guard"],[1,"60","3","Maritime Security Interagency Cooperation","strengthen cooperation and collaboration with the police, the Self-Defense Forces and overseas coast guard agencies","The Japan Coast Guard | the police | the Self-Defense Forces | overseas coast guard agencies"],[1,"60","3","Maritime Security Human Resources Development","secure and develop human resources based on the Policy on the Strengthening Maritime Security Capabilities","The Japan Coast Guard"],[1,"60","3","Satellite Constellation for Space Security","the government will strengthen comprehensive efforts related to space security, such as proceeding with necessary measures to build a satellite constellation",""],[1,"60","3","Counter-Disinformation and Strategic Communications Capacity","Japan will strengthen information warfare responses, including counter-disinformation measures that involve the strengthening of cooperation with agencies outside the government",""]],"79":[[1,"60","2","National Cybersecurity Capability Development","Japan will advance efforts in the areas that complement and are inseparable from the fundamental reinforcement of the defense capabilities, namely, cyber security",""],[1,"61","1","Cybersecurity Capability Strengthening","the government will strengthen cyber security capabilities",""],[1,"61","1","Active Cyber Defense Legislation","submit a bill at an early point in time to implement active cyber defense",""],[1,"61","1","Active Cyber Defense Implementation Systems","develop necessary systems156 for their proper implementation",""],[1,"61","1","Domestic Security Technology and GSOC Strengthening","we will utilize home-grown security technology and strengthen the functions of GSOC157",""],[1,"61","2","Government Shared Platform Cybersecurity Strengthening","the government will strengthen the security of the Government Shared Platform System",""],[1,"61","2","Critical Infrastructure Cybersecurity Exercises","conduct exercises on critical infrastructure through public-private partnerships",""],[1,"61","2","Cybersecurity Response Policy Penetration Testing","review response policies through practical penetration testing",""],[1,"61","2","Anti-Phishing Measures","strengthen anti-phishing measures",""],[1,"61","2","Cybersecurity Awareness and Human Resources Development","raising awareness, training and developing human resources related to cybersecurity",""],[1,"61","2","IoT Device Security Requirements Evaluation System","Starting in FY 2024, the government will work to diffuse the system for evaluating the soundness of security requirements for IoT devices",""],[1,"61","2","Third-Party IoT Security Evaluation System","in coordination with government procurement, will begin exploring a new system for a third-party organization to conduct evaluations",""]],"80":[[1,"64","1","Ship-Based Disaster Medical Care","promote medical care utilizing ships",""],[1,"64","1","Medical Container Deployment","utilize medical containers",""],[1,"64","1","Disaster Medical Care Continuity Initiative","ensure continuity of medical care by promoting dental visits and use of disaster medical systems in disaster-stricken areas",""],[1,"64","2","Regional Disaster Case Management Strengthening","efforts will be made to strengthen disaster case management",""],[1,"64","2","Disaster Victim Support Personnel Development","secure and train personnel to support disaster victims, including disaster intermediate support organizations",""],[1,"64","2","Flood, Landslide and Storm Surge Information Provision","provide information on floods, landslides and storm surge",""],[1,"64","2","Protection Measures for Vulnerable Evacuees","take measures for evacuees requiring special consideration",""],[1,"64","2","Cultural Property Disaster Prevention Measures","take disaster prevention measures to protect valuable cultural properties in local communities",""],[1,"64","2","Regional Fire and Disaster Prevention Capacity Enhancement","enhance fire and disaster prevention capabilities, including fire brigades",""],[1,"65","3","Life-Saving Emergency Relief","providing life-saving relief",""],[1,"65","3","Earthquake Road-Clearing Operations","road clearing",""],[1,"65","3","Push-Type Emergency Material Support","push-type material support",""],[1,"65","3","Secondary Evacuation Support","secondary evacuation support",""],[1,"66","1","Integrated Initial Disaster Response Mechanism","We will carry out the initial response by the police, firefighters, and the Self-Defense Forces, etc., provide support from the national government and related organizations to the affected municipalities and deliver the initial response by strengthening cooperation with medical and welfare personnel such as the Disaster Medical Assistance Team (DMAT) and other teams174, private businesses, specialized volunteer groups, etc.",""],[1,"66","1","Emergency Evacuation and Relief Operations","We will also strengthen other emergency disaster countermeasures such as support for the operation of evacuation centers, procurement and transportation of goods, wide-area and at-home evacuation, etc.175",""],[1,"66","1","Disaster-Time Digital Human Resources Development","digital human resources at the time of a disaster",""],[1,"66","1","Disaster Preparedness Awareness and Training","awareness building and practical training for disaster preparation",""],[1,"66","1","Disaster Response System Reviews","necessary system reviews",""],[1,"66","2","Drone-Based Disaster Situation Assessment","ascertaining the disaster situation by utilizing drones, etc.",""],[1,"66","2","Special Vehicle Disaster Area Access","strengthening approaches to the disaster area by utilizing special vehicles, etc.",""],[1,"66","2","Unmanned Robot Disaster Area Support","facilitating activities in the disaster area by utilizing unmanned robots, etc.",""],[1,"66","2","Disaster Supporter Activity Environment Enhancement","enhancing the activity environment for supporters",""],[1,"66","2","Emergency Water, Electricity, and Communications Provision","securing water, electricity, and communications by utilizing water-circulating showers, etc.",""],[1,"66","2","Emergency Health, Medical, and Welfare Support","enhancing health, medical care, and welfare",""],[1,"66","2","Mobile Vehicle and Container Disaster Support","utilizing mobile vehicles and containers for disaster support",""],[1,"66","2","Regional Disaster Crime Prevention Measures","enhancing regional crime prevention measures",""],[1,"66","2","Disaster Information Sharing and Unification System","sharing and unifying information by utilizing information and communication systems",""],[1,"66","2","Routine-Time Use of Disaster Technologies","We will also promote the utilization of these technologies and measures from normal times so that they can be effectively utilized during disasters.",""],[1,"66","4","Educational Personnel Disaster Dispatch Programme","Including the dispatch of educational personnel for school support at the time of disaster.",""],[1,"66","4","Welfare Integration into Disaster Systems","Including consideration of the positioning of welfare in disaster-related systems.",""],[1,"66","4","Evacuation Center Meal Stocking and Provision","Stocking and provision of meals at evacuation centers",""],[1,"66","4","Evacuation Center Cardboard Bed Partition Installation","installation of corrugated cardboard bed partitions",""],[1,"66","4","Evacuation Center Toilet Environment Improvement","improvement of toilet environments by utilizing self-propelled toilets and toilet trailers",""],[1,"66","4","Gender-Responsive Evacuation Center Operations","the operation of evacuation centers based on women's perspectives",""],[1,"66","4","Distributed System Review","Including examination of distributed systems.",""]],"81":[[1,"67","4","Economic Revitalization Support","made every effort to support the economy so as to revitalize it",""],[1,"68","1","Public-Private Partnership Investment Promotion","encouraging proactive investment through public-private partnerships",""],[1,"68","5","Productivity Improvement Measures","The government intends to raise the potential growth rate through improving productivity",""],[1,"68","5","Labor Force Participation Expansion","The government intends to raise the potential growth rate through ... expanding labor force participation",""],[1,"68","5","Birth Rate Increase Measures","The government intends to raise the potential growth rate through ... increasing the birth rate",""],[1,"68","5","Public-Private Domestic Investment Initiative","We will aggressively make domestic investment with the collective power of the public and private sectors",""],[1,"68","5","Corporate Investment Expansion Support","We will ... encourage the corporate sector to shift to excess investment to support growth on both the demand and supply sides",""],[1,"68","5","Integrated Economic, Fiscal, and Social Security Reform","We will advance integrated reforms in the economy, public finance, and social security, ensuring their coordinated advancement",""],[1,"69","1","DX-Enabled Productivity Improvement Initiative","social implementation of new technologies and productivity improvement through DX",""],[1,"69","1","Public-Private Planned Investment Promotion","Under public-private partnerships, the government will carry out policy management to promote medium- to long-term planned investment that will enhance the predictability of the private sector, stimulating aggressive and bold private sector investment.",""],[1,"70","4","Comprehensive Tax System Study for Structural Changes","we will conduct comprehensive studies to manifest the best tax system for coping with a declining birthrate, an aging population, globalization and other socioeconomic structural changes.",""],[1,"70","5","Ability-to-Pay Redistribution and Disparity Prevention","we will aim to improve redistribution functions based on the principle of ability to pay and prevent disparities from becoming fixed.",""],[1,"70","5","Fair Taxation for Diverse Work Styles and Digital Society","we will build a tax system that is fair and neutral to diverse work styles and suitable for a digital society",""],[1,"70","5","Overall Tax System Revenue Base Reform","we will revamp the overall tax system to secure a stable tax revenue base that does not hinder economic growth",""],[1,"70","5","National Evidence-Based Policymaking Strengthening Initiative","while steadily strengthening our efforts for EBPM.",""],[1,"70","5","Tax Settlement and Fair Taxation Enforcement Measures","we will step up efforts both in terms of the system and its enforcement and comply with new international taxation rules.",""],[1,"70","5","New International Taxation Rules Compliance Measures","comply with new international taxation rules.",""]],"82":[[1,"72","4","Physician Recruitment Plan Review","reviewing the physician recruitment plan",""],[1,"72","4","Regional Physician Training Quotas","utilizing regional quotas in the physician training process",""],[1,"72","4","Physician Dispatch to Underserved Regions","dispatching physicians",""],[1,"72","5","Elderly Medical Care and Assistance System Review","the government will further examine the ideal medical care system for the latter-stage elderly, which is currently administered by the wide-area federations, and the ideal medical assistance system that includes participation of public assistance recipients in national health insurance and the medical care system for the latter-stage elderly",""],[1,"73","1","Comprehensive Medical Care Physician Development","fostering physicians with comprehensive medical care capabilities",""],[1,"73","1","Recurrent Medical Education Programme","the implementation of recurrent education",""],[1,"73","1","Economic Incentives for Physician Redistribution","correcting the maldistribution through economic incentives",""],[1,"73","1","Regulatory Requirements for Medical Managers","drastically expanding the requirements for managers requiring experience of working in areas with a small number of physicians",""],[1,"73","1","FY 2026 Medical School Admission Quota Cap","the quota will be set within a range that does not exceed the comparable number in FY 2024",""],[1,"73","1","Future Medical School Admission Supply-Demand Review","the government will promptly examine the appropriateness",""],[1,"74","2","Comprehensive Medical Insurance System Reform","The government will proceed with comprehensive consideration of various medical insurance systems, including the submission of related legislative bills, while trying to balance benefits and burdens and restrain the rising burden on the working generation.",""],[1,"74","2","Medical Expense Rationalization by Reviewing Institutions","the government will strengthen efforts of the examining and paying institutions to rationalize medical expenses",""],[1,"74","2","Multiple Medication and Examination Rationalization Mechanism","will prepare an effective mechanism for rationalizing multiple drug administration and multiple examinations, etc.",""],[1,"74","2","Prefectural Health Insurance Premium Unification","we will thoroughly unify the level of insurance premiums within prefectures",""],[1,"74","2","National Health Insurance Insurer Function Strengthening","promote efforts to strengthen insurer functions",""],[1,"74","2","National Health Insurance Financial Support Mechanism Review","consider the ideal form of financial support such as adjustment subsidies and the insurer effort support system",""],[1,"74","2","Internationally Comparable Health Expenditure Statistics","We will also promote the preparation of health expenditure statistics that are internationally comparable",""],[1,"74","3","Long-Term Care User Burden Criteria Review","the government will review the criteria for determining the bracket of \"income above a certain level\" in which the user burden is set at 20%",""],[1,"74","3","Care Management Benefit Design Review","will discuss the ideal form of benefits related to care management",""],[1,"74","3","Livelihood Support Benefits Review for Mild Symptoms","the ideal form of benefits related to livelihood support services, etc., for persons with mild symptoms",""],[1,"74","4","Health Insurance Financing Balance Monitoring","Periodically visualize the balance between the insurance benefit rate (insurance premiums and public expenses) and the patient burden rate, etc.",""],[1,"74","4","Comprehensive Health Insurance Financing Measures","consider comprehensive measures for insurance premiums, public expenses, and patient payments.",""],[1,"74","4","OECD System of Health Accounts Data Compilation Study","Including the study for compiling data into the government statistics based on the System of Health Accounts (SHA) approach of the OECD.",""],[1,"75","1","Long-Term Care Remuneration System Review","reviewing the remuneration system",""],[1,"75","1","Long-Term Care Regulation Strengthening","strengthening regulations",""],[1,"75","1","Public Employment Placement Service Function Strengthening","further examining the strengthening of the function of public employment placement services",""],[1,"75","1","Flexible Care Service Environment for Working Carers","local governments will develop an environment for flexible operation, appropriate selection of services, and improvement of reliability, in order to promote the use of services not covered by the long-term care insurance system",""]],"83":[[1,"73","3","Comprehensive Disease Prevention and Health Promotion Measures","we will promote measures against cancer, against cardiovascular diseases, against hearing loss 186 , against intractable diseases, for transplant medicine 187 , against chronic kidney disease, against allergies 188 , against addiction 189, for nutrition, for sleep, against COPD, etc.",""],[1,"73","3","Infectious Disease Vaccination Measures","The government will also promote comprehensive measures to support women's health against menopause and osteoporosis, etc. In addition, we will use scientific evidence on general health and oral health and provide appropriate information to the public; promote specific initiatives for lifelong dental examinations (universal oral health checks); enhance oral health management by dental professionals helping to combat oral frailty and prevent",""],[1,"73","4","Early Hearing Loss Awareness and Hearing Aid Experience Programme","Includes creating opportunities for the elderly to realize their own hearing loss at an early stage and promoting the experience of hearing aids.",""],[1,"73","4","Organ Transplantation Medical Care Provision System","Including the construction of the medical care provision system for transplantation based on the increase in the number of organ donors.",""],[1,"73","4","Uniform Medical Care for Allergic Diseases","Including the promotion of uniformity of medical care for allergic diseases (Including atopic dermatitis).",""],[1,"73","4","Research and Studies Promotion Initiative","Including the promotion of research and studies, etc.",""],[1,"74","1","Dental Care Sector Collaboration Mechanism","promote collaboration among various occupations such as between dental institutions, and between medical, dental and pharmacological cooperation",""],[1,"74","1","Dental Health Workforce Security Measures","implement measures based on the necessity of securing dental hygienists and dental technicians",""],[1,"74","1","ICT Adoption in Dentistry","promote the use of ICT in the field of dentistry",""],[1,"74","1","Equitable Allocation of Dental Professionals","promote an appropriate allocation of dentists in each field",""],[1,"74","1","Dental Health Care System Development","thereby working to develop and improve systems for providing dental health care",""],[1,"74","1","Insurance Coverage for Approved Dental Innovations","promote the introduction to the relevant insurance systems for new technologies and new materials that have been approved as effective and safe",""],[1,"74","1","ICT-Enabled Home-Visit Care Workforce Programme","the government will promote measures to secure home-visit long-term care and nurses through the use of ICT and specific action training",""],[1,"74","1","Multifunctional Home Medical and Long-Term Care Services","promote home medical care and long-term care through multifunctional home services",""],[1,"74","1","Rehabilitation for Self-Reliance and Social Reintegration","promote rehabilitation that contributes to self-reliance and social reintegration",""],[1,"75","2","Salt Reduction Promotion Initiative","the government will collaborate with private companies in promoting salt reduction, etc.",""],[1,"75","2","Passive Smoking Prevention Measures","will advance measures against unwanted passive smoking.",""],[1,"75","2","Collaborative Health and Cancer Screening Initiative","we will deepen collaboration between insurers and employers (collaborative health) based on the Third Term Data Health Plan in order to contribute to an increase in cancer screening rates.",""],[1,"75","2","Serious Illness Prevention Demonstration Research","we will promote the creation of health services and health care services by utilizing large-scale demonstration research projects on the prevention of the onset and progression of serious illness, and health promotion",""],[1,"75","2","AMED Evidence Translation Capacity Strengthening","we will strengthen the functions of the Japan Agency for Medical Research and Development (AMED) toward the effective use of the obtained evidence in society.",""],[1,"75","2","Community-Based Long-Term Care Prevention Services","the government will promote measures for effectively preventing the onset of long-term care by enhancing community support projects, thereby promoting flexible services provided by various local entities.",""],[1,"75","2","Evidence-Based Integrated Long-Term Care","We will also promote evidence-based scientific long-term care and will establish an appropriate care cycle between medical care and long-term care.",""],[1,"75","2","Personal Health Record Integration Initiative","PHR, including life-log data (sleep, step count, etc.) recorded in wearable devices, will be utilized eyeing the possibility to collaborate with medical care and long-term care.",""],[1,"75","2","Health Promotion Service Quality Visualization","The government will also encourage private organizations to implement \"visualization of quality\" in their health promotion services.",""],[1,"76","1","International Clinical Trial and Drug Manufacturing System","we will work to develop an internationally competitive clinical trial system that can conduct First-in Human (FIH) studies of innovative drug candidates; review the approval requirements for core clinical research core hospitals; develop a manufacturing system for investigational drugs and biopharmaceuticals; and develop and secure human resources.",""],[1,"76","1","Medical Data and Genome Data Utilization Policy","the government will clarify the interpretation of some genome data that are not personally identifiable under the Personal Information Protection Act.",""],[1,"76","1","Public-Private Drug Discovery Ecosystem Coordination","the government will connect various players from academia to industry through the invitation of foreign companies and VCs by public-private councils, and will reorganize the drug discovery ecosystem, including the development of the promotion system, so that new R&D funds can be invested in each stage, including the early stage.",""],[1,"76","1","University Hospital Drug Discovery Research Support","We will also drastically strengthen drug discovery capabilities by improving the environment for enhancing R&D capabilities of university hospitals, etc., and strengthening the research infrastructure through R&D support of AMED.",""]],"84":[[1,"76","1","Combined Medical Expenses and Private Insurance Review","the government will proceed with deliberations on the ideal system of combined medical expenses outside insurance, including the utilization of private insurances.",""],[1,"76","1","Drug Loss and Software as a Medical Device Regulation","The government will consider regulatory measures to deal with drug losses, etc., and to promote the implementation of Software as a Medical Device, and will reach a conclusion by the end of 2024.",""],[1,"76","1","Pharmaceutical Approval Review Enhancement","We will also promote the enhancement of the approval review and consultation systems.",""],[1,"76","1","International Harmonization of Pharmaceutical Regulations","At the same time, efforts will be made to promote harmonization of pharmaceutical regulations utilizing overseas bases of the Pharmaceuticals and Medical Device Agency (PMDA).",""],[1,"76","1","Pharmaceutical Cost-Effectiveness Assessment Reform","We will study ways to make better use of cost-effectiveness assessment—including appropriate evaluation of the innovativeness of pharmaceuticals—in terms of promoting innovations and giving consideration to the burden of insurance contributions on the working population, while maintaining the operation for prompt NHI listing.",""],[1,"76","1","Treatment Effectiveness Research and Clinical Guidelines","we will encourage research and studies on effective and efficient treatment, including drug suspension and reduction, and will reflect such outcomes in clinical practice guidelines.",""],[1,"76","1","Pharmaceutical Supply Stabilization Measures","The government will work to resolve the current concerns about the supply of pharmaceuticals.",""],[1,"77","1","Pharmaceutical Industry Structural Reform and Supply Framework","we will promote structural reforms with a view to industry restructuring and will put into a place the relevant legal framework for a stable supply of pharmaceuticals",""],[1,"77","1","Biosimilar Use Promotion","we will promote the use of biosimilars, etc.",""],[1,"77","1","Self-Care and Self-Medication Promotion","we will encourage self-care and self-medication, through the further promotion of switch OTC, etc.",""],[1,"77","1","Review of Drug Self-Pay Arrangements","we will proceed with deliberations on the review of the self-pay portion for drugs",""],[1,"77","1","FY 2025 Drug Price Survey and Revision Review","The government will explore what the drug price survey and revision for FY 2025 should look like",""],[1,"77","2","Flat-Rate Drug Self-Payment Reform","The Reform Process describes \"flat-rate self-pay portion for drugs\"",""],[1,"77","2","Drug-Type-Based Self-Payment Reform","The Reform Process describes \"establishment of self-pay portion according to the type of drugs\"",""],[1,"77","2","Drug Insurance Benefits Review","The Reform Process describes \"review of insurance benefits for drugs similar to marketed products.\"",""],[1,"78","1","Healthcare Transformation Regulatory Reform","In the healthcare field, we will take policy measures, including regulatory reform, with the aim of promoting HX (Healthcare Transformation) and expanding investment.",""],[1,"78","1","Refill Prescription Promotion Initiative","In order to promote the use of refill prescriptions, we will closely examine the hindrance factors and work to build momentum, such as by raising the awareness of individual insurers.",""],[1,"77","1","Pharmaceutical and Medical Device Product Database","build a product database for pharmaceuticals and medical devices",""]],"85":[[1,"77","1","Domestic Antimicrobial Supply Framework","the government will consider a framework for the development of an environment in which domestically manufactured APIs (active pharmaceutical ingredients) can be used continuously, as well as measures to ensure a certain volume of domestic distribution",""],[1,"77","1","Antimicrobial Development Market Incentives and Research","the government, industry, and academia will cooperate to secure drugs for the treatment of drug-resistant bacteria through market incentives for the development of new antimicrobial agents and research projects",""],[1,"77","1","Innovative Drug Research for Emerging Infectious Diseases","research projects to promote the development of innovative drugs for emerging and re-emerging infectious diseases",""],[1,"77","1","International Antimicrobial Research Collaboration","will promote international collaboration on antimicrobial agent research and development support",""]],"86":[[1,"77","1","Healthcare Startup Development and Support","we will strongly promote the development and support of healthcare startups in the medical and long-term care field",""],[1,"77","1","Whole Genome Analysis Information Infrastructure","prepare an information infrastructure through the Whole Genome Analysis Implementation Plan",""],[1,"77","1","Whole Genome Analysis Results Utilization System","put into place a system for the utilization of analysis results such as feedback to patients",""],[1,"77","1","Drug Discovery Artificial Intelligence Platform","develop a drug discovery AI platform for drug discovery",""],[1,"77","1","Healthcare Industry and Regenerative Medicine Promotion","promote the healthcare industry, including medical devices, as well as R&D on drug discovery using iPS cells and regenerative medicine, etc.",""],[1,"77","1","Healthcare Industrial Promotion Bases","develop industrial promotion bases related to this field",""],[1,"77","2","Medical Innovation Support Office","Medical venture total support office named “MEDical Innovation Support Office.”",""],[1,"77","2","CARe Innovation Support Consultation Office","CARe Innovation Support Office (CARISO) serves as a consultation desk.",""],[1,"77","2","Whole Genome Analysis Implementation Plan","Whole Genome Analysis Implementation Plan 2022 (the Ministry of Health, Labor and Welfare, September 30, 2022).","Ministry of Health, Labor and Welfare"],[1,"77","2","Integrated Drug Discovery AI Platform","A platform that develops multiple drug discovery AIs (containing information on ligands (such as antibodies that recognize cancer cells)) and integrates them.",""],[1,"78","1","Pseudonymized Medical Information Research Promotion","The government will promote the utilization of the Next Generation Medical Infrastructure Act203 in order to promote research and development using pseudonymized medical information.",""],[1,"78","1","Domestic Medical Radioisotope Production Systems","Regarding radioisotopes for medical use, the government will promote the engagement based on the Action Plan204, such as by putting into place the necessary systems for domestic production 205 , and will discuss the relevant matters206 toward the revision of the Action Plan.",""]],"87":[[1,"78","1","School-Based Blood Donation Awareness Programme","Understanding of blood donation shall be deepened through promotion about blood donation at the elementary and junior high school level.",""],[1,"78","1","Domestic Blood Product Supply Programme","With regard to blood products and plasma derived products such as globulin and fibrinogen, we will promote the domestic self-sufficient supply, stable securing, and proper use.",""]],"88":[[1,"78","3","Public Pension System Revision","the government will draw up a course of action for the system revision by the end of 2024 based on the results of the Actuarial Valuation this summer",""],[1,"78","3","Expansion of Employees’ Insurance Coverage","the thorough expansion of the application of employees’ insurance to part-time workers",""],[1,"78","3","Removal of Enterprise-Size Requirement for Insurance Coverage","the abolition of the requirement for the size of enterprises",""],[1,"78","3","Removal of Industry Exclusions for Single-Person Establishments","the elimination of industries that are not covered",""],[1,"78","3","Annual Income Barrier Support Package","the promotion of utilization of the package for not being conscious of so-called “annual income barriers”",""],[1,"79","2","Work-Style-Neutral Social Security System","build a social security system that is neutral corresponding to work styles",""],[1,"79","2","Lifelong Participation Environment","create an environment where people can fulfill their potential throughout their lives regardless of their age or gender",""],[1,"79","3","Social Security Structural Reform Research","the government will conduct research on structural reforms aimed at stabilizing the medium- to long-term social security system and ensuring peace of mind",""]],"89":[[1,"79","1","Community Health and Child-Rearing Model Project","Model Project (tentative name) in the fields of health and medical care as well as child-rearing support in specific community fields",""],[1,"79","1","Cross-Vertical Policy Coordination Mechanism","under policy coordination that transcends vertical divisions",""],[1,"79","1","All-Generations Preventive Health Checkup Programme","we will promote proactive care through health checkups for all generations",""],[1,"79","1","Wearable-Enabled Future Health Care Model","verify a future-oriented health care model that takes into account the utilization of health data through the use of wearable devices",""],[1,"79","2","Additional Health Incentives","the government will provide additional health incentives",""],[1,"79","1","Existing Project Utilization Measures","consider measures from the perspective of effective utilization of existing projects",""]],"90":[[1,"81","2","Child Poverty Food and Learning Support Programme","supporting children's restaurants, meal deliveries for children, outreach assistance, and their learning, as well as by providing experiential opportunities",""],[1,"81","2","Child and Family Monitoring Strengthening Mechanism","the strengthening of monitoring roles",""],[1,"81","2","Child and Family Center System Strengthening","strengthening the system of child and family centers",""],[1,"81","2","Family Support Services Expansion","enhancing and promoting the use of family support services",""],[1,"81","2","Family-Based Care and Foster Support Programme","thoroughly implementing the principle of giving priority to family rearing, including the enhancement of support by foster parents and family homes",""],[1,"81","2","Social Care Leaver Self-Reliance Support","enhancing self-reliance support for those with experience of social care, etc.",""],[1,"81","2","Temporary Shelter Environment Improvement","improving the environment of temporary shelters",""],[1,"82","1","Young Carer Support Programme","Support for young carers will be promoted",""],[1,"82","1","Child and Youth Shelter Support Programme","enhancing support for shelters for children/youths as well as young people facing difficulties due to abuse",""],[1,"82","1","Child Guidance Center Capacity Strengthening","strengthening the system of child guidance centers such as child welfare officers in terms of quality and quantity",""],[1,"82","1","Foster Home Nurturing and Environment Improvement","improving the nurturing functions and environment of foster homes.",""],[1,"82","1","Inclusive Support System for Children with Disabilities","The government will develop support systems for all children with disabilities, including children with developmental disabilities and children under medical care, and will promote inclusion.",""],[1,"82","1","Nationwide Children's Hospice Expansion","We will also promote efforts toward the nationwide spread of children's hospices.",""],[1,"82","1","Single-Parent Family Support Programme","The government will promote support for single parents, including employment support, child rearing allowance, and secure payment of child support and the promotion of safe and secure visitation or other contact between the parent and the child through support service for parents before/after divorce.",""],[1,"82","1","Revised Civil Code Dissemination and Judicial Environment Reform","We will also disseminate the revised Civil Code217 and work with the judicial branch to improve the environment.",""],[1,"82","1","Free School Meals Policy Study","We will study the challenges regarding free school meals.",""]],"91":[[1,"84","1","ICT-Enabled Education and Welfare Consultation System","We will also strengthen the use of ICT and cooperation between education and welfare, developing an environment in which people can consult with SC and SSW, etc., as well as the police at any time",""],[1,"84","1","Yogo Teacher Support System","promoting the support system for yogo teachers",""],[1,"84","1","School Safety Promotion Programme","promoting school safety that incorporates the concept of safety promotion schools",""],[1,"84","1","Student Physical Strength and Vision Improvement Measures","We will also strengthen measures to stop the decline in physical strength and vision",""],[1,"84","1","School Food and Dental Health Education","will promote food education centered on nutrition teachers and dental health education",""],[1,"84","2","Special Needs Education Class Management","Includes proper management of special needs education classes",""],[1,"84","2","Safe School Commuting Measures","Includes safety measures for commuting to school such as the use of school buses",""],[1,"84","2","School Facility Disaster Preparedness Strengthening","Includes the strengthening of disaster preparedness functions such as the installation of air conditioning equipment in gymnasiums",""],[1,"84","2","School Facility Lifecycle and Decarbonization Renovation","longer service life/decarbonization renovations that integrate improvements to the educational environment with countermeasures against deterioration",""],[1,"84","2","Special Needs School Classroom Capacity Expansion","planned and efficient development initiatives such as efforts to eliminate the shortage of classrooms at special needs education schools",""]],"92":[[1,"87","2","Construction Workforce Recruitment and Training","the government will secure and train workers",""],[1,"87","2","Women's Active Participation in Construction","developing an environment for women's active participation",""],[1,"87","2","Construction Industry Work-Style Reform","promoting work-style reforms",""],[1,"87","2","Construction Industry Safety Management","ensuring safety management",""]],"93":[[1,"87","3","PPP/PFI Public Service Delivery Expansion","With regard to PPP/PFI, which will provide public services efficiently and effectively, we will further advance efforts with the aim of steadily achieving the targets set forth in the revised Action Plan231.",""],[1,"87","3","Priority-Area PPP Project Development Support","While continuing to support the business development of PPP projects in priority areas such as water PPPs, airports, stadiums/arenas, etc., we will promote PPP/PFI for SDF facilities, national parks, and crematoriums.",""],[1,"87","3","Private-Sector PPP Incentive Environment","In addition to building an environment in which private companies can obtain appropriate profits through their efforts and ingenuity, we will promote the creation of cross-sectoral and wide-area projects.",""],[1,"87","3","Local PPP Platform Strengthening","We will ... strengthen local platforms.",""],[1,"89","2","Local Community Human Resources Development Programme","Local governments will work together to promote efforts to secure and train human resources necessary for local communities.",""],[1,"89","2","Joint Wide-Area Administrative Service Delivery","Related ministries and agencies as well as local governments will also work together to jointly implement administrative works where wide-area efforts are considered effective.",""],[1,"89","2","Shared Public Facilities Consolidation Initiative","We will reinforce efforts for consolidation or joint use of public facilities among several local governments.",""],[1,"89","2","Interlocal Cooperation for Daily Life Services","In addition, we will progressively develop an environment that facilitates the provision of daily life services through cooperation and collaboration among various local entities.",""]],"97":[[1,"88","4","Regional Disaster Prevention and Mitigation Strengthening","We will also strengthen respective regions' own disaster prevention and mitigation efforts based on the lessons learned from the 2024 Noto Peninsula Earthquake",""]]}});